round his neck. while a box lay at his\n1476\tfeet within reach-he was a suicide\n1477\t/ His distorted features and glaring eyes\n1478\twere plainly visible, while his tongue.\n1479\tblack and swollen. hung at least half a\n1480\tfoot from his month To complete the\n1481\thorrible picture. hundreds of demons\n1482\ttod\n1483\tThen followed wild burst of laughter\n1484\tand the apparition vanished.\n1485\tThe young men had not expected this.\n1486\tWhile this strange scene was enactmg\n1487\tthey sat stUpefied with fear, their hair\n1488\tactually standing on end.\n1489\t\n1490\t\n1491\tAt length their horrible spell was\n1492\tbroken, and without even stopping to\n1493\tsnatch their hats, they fled the house\n1494\tAs they were fleeing along the street.\n1495\tthey ran right into the arms of tall,\n1496\tmuScUlaTman, who seeing their alright\n1497\ted condition. frightened his grasp upon\n1498\tthem, and asked them to explain their\n1499\tfright.\n1500\t\n1501\t\n1502\tThey told him all.\n1503\t\n1504\t\n1505\tAfter they had finished their story,\n1506\tthe detective for it was no other than\n1507\tDetective John Burnside. of New \\ Ork.\n1508\twho was visiting friends there told\n1509\tthem Ito say nothing about it, but wait\n1510\tand hope and he would discover the\n1511\tmystery if possible\n1512\t\n1513\t\n1514\tAbout two weeks after the detective\n1515\treturned hOme-so his friends thought.\n1516\t\n1517\t\n1518\tIn course of time the young men dis\n1519\tcovered that they conld no longer keep\n1520\tthe secret. and 50 they divulged it.\n1521\t\n1522\t\n1523\t1t raised great excitement, of course,\n1524\tand the people Of the city gave the place\n1525\ta wide berth.\n1526\t\n1527\t\n1528\tThe strange sounds and sights We're\n1529\tcontinued. until the people believed\n1530\twithout a doubt that the house was\n1531\thaunted.\n1532\t\n1533\t\n1534\tWe Will pass over year.\n1535\t\n1536\t\n1537\tOne morning a posse of police, headed\n1538\tby Il tall man in plain