ey have, seems inaccessible 10 hide\nIN, which protect them from pursuit Globe.\n\n\nDispatches from Major General Scott dated Anil ~\nat Tampa Bay, have been received the Adutant Ce-\nneraIs Office, from which the following extracts are\nmade:\n\n\nhave the honor 10 report for the information Of the\nSecretary of War, and General-in Chief reached\ntins place with the greater part OF the right wing under\nGeneral Eustis came in win iaif of The len VIM, H.\nsame day. and Col Lindsay, who commands the centre\nthe day before This approximation of the greater parts\nOh ihe three Columns was the result of particular in\nsructions Each found itself compelled TO come in for\nsubsistence\n\n\nThe reports of those principal commanders, under me-\nand G.. - -\n1t will be seen, that although no general battle has\nbeen fought many combas and sharp affairs have taken\nThe report states that far from the enemy hov;no\nbeen besten and compelled TO for peace on the con-\nary, \" small parties which ha We been met with nlos,\nevery where, have ercely resisted until put in dancer\nOF the bayonet The war, on part fact scarce\nly bcgun.\"\n\n\nand saddle, were much reduced-many broke down on\nthe march, owing TO the bad of the roads boi wea\nther, great loads, and Indifferent grazing Sickness,\nmeases and mumps) has considerably reduced the ef\nfeetive force.\n\n\nThe Central states that Colonel Smith with his Loui.\nsiana Tcgimnt was about 10 proceed Charotles har-\nDor and Pease creek. There he be Joined by ma\nval officer, and proceeding up the creek land on The left\nbank On the 18th April Colonel Goodwin's haunted\nSouth Caroqa volunteers 1--WE hundred strong) was 10\nmarch 1m Tampa Boy for the upper part of Pear creek\nfollowed by he foot of General Euslis wing The OBJ\nject Of the ombned 10 strike AT the ne.\ngroes, women children, and warriors who settle\nments on fhe upper and lower part Of the creek and\nwho are POW IN securiy supposed 10 be engaged in\nplanting, fishing, and hunting\"\n\n\nCuond Lindsay, with battalion of United States mr.\ntery, company of Georgia mounted men the Alabama\nregImenb and an independent company of Louisiana\nvoluntcfrsis at the time, march northwardly in\npursuitot the Indians also, General Clinch with his\nc)mnand, both by different routes Colonel Lindsay\nvii eper the forks of the Withlacoochee and the nee\npenetrate practicable, far the head of the core\nwhilst GENERAL Cnch enters it below. Colonel Lind\nsay IS 10 scour the country, and penetrate the\ntufer than has heretofore been in tho power OF troops\nto 10.\n\n\nFurther operations Of course, will depend upon events\nyot yet developed\n\n\nfDufng the recent movement of the several columns\nand their various operations Of the troops 3 we're killed\nnnd 70 wounded The number Of Indians killed is sup\nposed to be ~.\n\n\nThe face Of the country inerspcrsed with bammocks,\ncypress swamps and marshes almost mpenerabc to the\nwhiinan, presents serious obstacles 10 Che prosecution\nOF ahpagn in Florida; and while these Businesses con.\nsent difficulties almost insurmountable 10 their indcia\ngable pursuers\n\n\nThree hundred and ninety nine (390) friendly Indians\n(one-thrd warror) reported 10 be board the trans\nports, for their destination in the West\n\n\nA..\n\n\nTExTRAcT1\n\n\n~. D. ttrr Usagty I'LL. n.\n\n=== 3_1920-04-18_p1_sn87055779_00296021477_1920041801_0544.json\nSouth Bend news-times. (South Bend, Ind.) 1913-1938 · 1920-04-18\ncrops: cached\nheadline: Castle\n---\nThe Blue Pearl. mystery, intrigue\nlove and revenge vie with each other\n10 hold the spectators interest revet-\ned right up until the dramatic eli\nmax A valuable pearl, is hid by\nits rightful owner. who hopes thus\nto prevent a sensational divorce.\nand the search that results lends.\nspeedy action TO the story. Edith\nHallOr Is the star.\n\n\nThe spirit of 1920 has crept into\nthe filming Of George Barr Nc\nCutcheon's novel \"A Fool and His\nMoney\" which is the Castles pictured\nattraction for tomorrow and Tues\nday. First the ouija board, then\nIeap-year, both incidents striking a\nresponsive chord with present-da\naudiences. Eugene OBrien is the\nstar while prominent in his support\nis charming Ruby DeRemer, who\nwill be remembered for her work in\nRex Beach's THE Auction Block\"\n\n\nMore powerful. more elaborate,\nmore gripping than any OF the\nJrevious Rex Beach feature pictures.\nis his latest Offering TO the silent\ndrama. Entitled The Girl From\nOutside\" and with its action laying\nI'm the great Klondyke region. il\ncomes 10 the Castle screen Wednes-\nday on Thursday Elsie Janis is\nstarred In The Imp\" which is said\nto give her even a better role than\ndid a Regular Girl\" J. Warren\nKerrigan is Fridays star in Live\nSparks\" while on Saturday the at\ntraction is Wallace Reid in Double\nSpeed\"\n\n=== 10_1845-04-07_p2_sn83030213_00206530212_1845040701_0535.json\nNew-York daily tribune. · 1845-04-07\ncrops: cached\nheadline: \n---\nGu- Wings Of the FIRST, FIrru, ElGurn, NINru,\nand SEVENTEENTH Wards, foa oin sce,st UhiS\nCommom Co,ecil # yon ,eiR. The issue is in your\nhands this moment. Take hold this moruing-See\nyour old brethren who have been led of on false\nscen,--imp!oye them 10 stand by the Good Old\nCause--show them that Nativisra has no,a ghost of\nchance. while the Wings have a lair prospect, and\nyou ,riR carry the City, There are coed hopes of\nother Wards beside our own SEcoNp, TtIEp and\nF,l.rErSra; but yours n.uy DC made s,9t. Each of\nthem bui the Seventeenth gave HsNry CLAY ma\n,or;y, and in the Seventeenth Nauvism is dying\nand Loco. .Focoism all in snarl. Take hold to-\nday. and secure WaiG GouNc,t and real City\nReform All together now\n\n=== 6_1927-11-08_pna_sn85042243_00199918679_1927110801_0541.json\nThe Bismarck tribune. [volume] (Bismarck, N.D.) 1916-current · 1927-11-08\ncrops: cached\nheadline: COACHING NOT\n\n\nTO BE CAREER\n\n\nOF RED GRANGE\n\n'Galloping Ghost Turns\nThumbs Down on Proposal\n\n\nto Be Grid Mentor\n---\nNew York, Nov. S.-lF-Eed\nGrange today turned thumbs down\non the idea of ever becoming a foot\nball coach.\n\n\nIf there's anybody in the world\nwho takes more grief in the form Of\ncriticism than the president Of the\nUnited States\" said Red. cts the\ncoach of college football team.\nNone Of that for mine.\"\n\n\nTo Make Another Movie\n\n\nWith his fiery thatch on a pillow\nwhile the coach and trainer of his\nNew York Yankees wrapped steam\ning wooden blankets around his right\nleg, Red allowed he'd stay at the\nprofessional game few years more.\nThis year he expects also to make\nanother movie or two.\n\n\n\"Of course\" the recumbent Gal\nLooping Ghost\" went on with a glance\nat the wool blankets under which\nlay one of his greatest assets, now\nslightly impaired by a stubborn case\nOF water on the knee, ut all depends\non how a man takes care of himself\nand whether he gets hurt\"\n\n\nThe leader Of the Yankees ex-\npected to play today at the Polo\nGrounds against the Chicago Bears,\ndespite his bad knee. It was in q\ngame with the league-leading Bears\nthree weeks ago that Grange suf-\nfered the injury which has kept him\noff the gridiron since.\n\n\nut was purely accidental -\nGrange declared Of this first serious\nmishap that has overtaken him in\nhis long football career, collegiate\nand professional. It occurred when\nTrait n. ex-Notre Dame star and\ncenter for the Bears, ran into him\nin a race for a forward pass.\n\n\nFunny in this pro game\" Red\npursued his horizontal reflections\n''These fellows who were all Amer.\nleans in college aren't half 50 tough\nas some of these birds from small\ncolleges that you never heard Of.\n\n\nAge Doesn't Count\n\n\n\"Another thing-age doesn't seen\nto count. There are a lot of fel.\nlows of IS and SO years old playing\nfootball in this league that we'd b\nmighty glad to get on the Yankees\n","numLines":1783,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1783}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c64e2733-9d4e-4b69-b57f-60