dinary Influence.\n307\t---\n308\tBERLIN, Nov 26.-Perhaps the\n309\tmost powerful man in Russia at\n310\tthe present moment is Rector The\n311\tophan, of the Ecclesiastical Acad-\n312\tenvy in St. Petersburg, known pop\n313\tularly as the monk of the Car. \"\n314\tTheophan, a professor Of theology,\n315\tIS, comparatively speaking, a\n316\tyoung man, tall of stature with\n317\tpiercing black eyes. whose Charac-\n318\tter is strongly impregnated with\n319\tmysticism. Up to the present he\n320\thas not come prominently before\n321\tthe public, but owing to the extra\n322\tordinary influence that he yields\n323\tover the Gar, he has become the\n324\tcentre of a circle of fawning cour-\n325\ttiers and syCophants\n326\t\n327\t\n328\tAbout a year ago Theophan was\n329\tsurprised to receive an invitation\n330\tfrom Grand Duke Peter NicChala-\n331\twitch, with whom he was aCquaint-\n332\ted through Prince Putiatkin, to be\n333\tpresented to the Gar, From that\n334\tmoment a new lite commenced for\n335\tthe monk, who found in the weak\n336\tGar an enthusiastic disciple.\n337\t\n338\t\n339\tThe Gar was charmed with the\n340\tquiet and decided manner of the\n341\tyoung man and the conversation\n342\tturned, during the course of many\n343\tsubsequent visits, from religion to\n344\tbelief, from belief to miracles, and\n345\trom miracles to mysticism, a sub\n346\tjeCt for which the Gar has shown\n347\tpenchant of late years.\n348\t\n349\t\n350\tAt first Theophan only visited\n351\tthe Gar when he was summoned,\n352\tbut he soon received the permis-\n353\tsion to 60 in and out of the I'M\n354\tperial Palaces when ever he desir-\n355\ted. The encourage of the Car\n356\tsoon discovered that Theophan\n357\thad developed into a parsonage in\n358\twhom the Gar placed implicit\n359\tconfidence, and with whom he fire.\n360\tquently discussed matters, towards\n361\twhich he manifested great reserve\n362\twhen with his ministers.\n363\t\n364\t\n365\tAt first only private matters\n366\tformed the gist of their conversa-\n367\ttions but>Itstc CT -si4~-thc monk was\n368\tConsulted concerning political af-\n369\tfairs and was able to obtain favors\n370\tthat the Gar even refused his\n371\town mother.\n372\t\n373\t\n374\tThus, some time ago the Gar\n375\tdismissed Prince Obolenski,\n376\tyouthful playmate, from the post\n377\tas chief Of his Cabinet. This\n378\tspelled ruined to the Prince, who\n379\tpossesses no means. Owing to the\n380\tintervention of the monk the Car\n381\tarranged that his salary of 10000\n382\trubles be paid till the prince dies,\n383\talthough he had refused the re-\n384\tquest of his mother to pension the\n385\tPrince. The Gar has further\n386\tmade prinCely gifts, lately for &c\n387\tclesiastical and charitable pur-\n388\tposes, solely at the instigation of\n389\tMonk Theophan\n390\t\n391\t\n392\tThe closest bond existing be\n393\ttween the Monk and the Gar is\n394\tthat OF mysticism That the Gar\n395\tis extremely accessible to such in\n396\thuence can be amply proved by\n397\tthe case Of Monseigneur Philippe\n398\twho played such an important role\n399\tat Zaraskoie Selo at the beginning\n400\tof the century, and who was dis\n401\tmissed from the court, laden with\n402\tn dllNI ICllllCl / SIN Z lldu\n403\tseverely demonstrated with the\n404\tGar concerning the influence that\n405\tthe Monseigneur exerted in poll\n406\ttics.\n407\t\n408\t\n409\tGrand Duke Peter and Princess\n410\tMilitia Nikolajevna are RESPONSE\n411\tbic for the introduction of this\n412\tgentleman with his seances and\n413\tapparitions to the Russian court.\n414\t\n415\t\n416\tThe extraordinary power that\n417\tthe Gear Monk\" has gained over\n418\tEmperor Nicholas has just been\n419\tevidenced anew by the fact that,\n420\twhereas all ecclesiastics were de-\n421\tbarred from being present at the\n422\tlaying of the foundation stone of\n423\tthe new regimental chapel at Ear\n424\taSkOie Selo. two DAYS before the\n425\t\n426\t=== 29_1910-10-28_p1_sn83045433_0010