n for the fatherland\n1100\tAZ he left the cafe London acquaint-\n1101\tance dropped into his vacant chair and\n1102\twhispered. DO you know the man\n1103\twith whom you were talking?\"\n1104\t\n1105\t\n1106\tNO.\" replied. but like his brand\n1107\tOf cigar\"\n1108\t\n1109\t\n1110\tWELL\" said my Englishman. be\n1111\tware OF him; he is a German secret\n1112\tagent who poses as an American\" ~\n1113\t\n1114\t\n1115\tl thanked him for his warming ac-\n1116\tcepted . cigar from him. too. and was\n1117\ttold next morning that he also Is\n1118\tGerman agent.\n1119\t\n1120\t\n1121\tThis is no place for another limo\n1122\tcent Abroad\" was my thought, and\n1123\tquickly left for The Hague. only to\n1124\tfind that had stepped from the fry\n1125\ting pan into the fire.\n1126\t\n1127\t\n1128\tHere have obtained firstAand\n1129\tknowledge of the wonderful German\n1130\tintelligence service which has succeed\n1131\ted after nearly two years persistent\n1132\tunremitting labor. in converting a sec\n1133\tton of the population-whose pockets\n1134\thave been hit by the blockade-to\n1135\tantf-Brftish. though not pro-German\n1136\tviews.\n1137\t\n1138\t\n1139\t\"Gott strafe England\"\n1140\t\n1141\t\n1142\t1t must be said. however, that as\n1143\tgeneral rule these propagandists are\n1144\tshrewder than the agents who were d.\n1145\trected by Doctor Dernburg. in the\n1146\tUnited States. and they have concen-\n1147\trated their energies in the promotion\n1148\tOf Colt strafe England\" sentiment\n1149\tamong the Dutch. II they have not\n1150\tsucceeded to the extent hoped for by\n1151\tBerlin. 1t is due. not to lack of zeal or\n1152\teffort. but to the common sense of the\n1153\tDutch government and people, who,\n1154\twhen the German agents charge that\n1155\tthe English blockade is forcing the\n1156\tworkers Of the country into idleness\n1157\tand compelling the inhabitants to eat\n1158\twar bread\" reply that. while England\n1159\tis undoubtedly partly to blame for the\n1160\