comparatively speaking, a\nyoung man, tall of stature with\npiercing black eyes. whose Charac-\nter is strongly impregnated with\nmysticism. Up to the present he\nhas not come prominently before\nthe public, but owing to the extra\nordinary influence that he yields\nover the Gar, he has become the\ncentre of a circle of fawning cour-\ntiers and syCophants\n\n\nAbout a year ago Theophan was\nsurprised to receive an invitation\nfrom Grand Duke Peter NicChala-\nwitch, with whom he was aCquaint-\ned through Prince Putiatkin, to be\npresented to the Gar, From that\nmoment a new lite commenced for\nthe monk, who found in the weak\nGar an enthusiastic disciple.\n\n\nThe Gar was charmed with the\nquiet and decided manner of the\nyoung man and the conversation\nturned, during the course of many\nsubsequent visits, from religion to\nbelief, from belief to miracles, and\nrom miracles to mysticism, a sub\njeCt for which the Gar has shown\npenchant of late years.\n\n\nAt first Theophan only visited\nthe Gar when he was summoned,\nbut he soon received the permis-\nsion to 60 in and out of the I'M\nperial Palaces when ever he desir-\ned. The encourage of the Car\nsoon discovered that Theophan\nhad developed into a parsonage in\nwhom the Gar placed implicit\nconfidence, and with whom he fire.\nquently discussed matters, towards\nwhich he manifested great reserve\nwhen with his ministers.\n\n\nAt first only private matters\nformed the gist of their conversa-\ntions but>Itstc CT -si4~-thc monk was\nConsulted concerning political af-\nfairs and was able to obtain favors\nthat the Gar even refused his\nown mother.\n\n\nThus, some time ago the Gar\ndismissed Prince Obolenski,\nyouthful playmate, from the post\nas chief Of his Cabinet. This\nspelled ruined to the Prince, who\npossesses no means. Owing to the\nintervention of the monk the Car\narranged that his salary of 10000\nrubles be paid till the prince dies,\nalthough he had refused the re-\nquest of his mother to pension the\nPrince. The Gar has further\nmade prinCely gifts, lately for &c\nclesiastical and charitable pur-\nposes, solely at the instigation of\nMonk Theophan\n\n\nThe closest bond existing be\ntween the Monk and the Gar is\nthat OF mysticism That the Gar\nis extremely accessible to such in\nhuence can be amply proved by\nthe case Of Monseigneur Philippe\nwho played such an important role\nat Zaraskoie Selo at the beginning\nof the century, and who was dis\nmissed from the court, laden with\nn dllNI ICllllCl / SIN Z lldu\nseverely demonstrated with the\nGar concerning the influence that\nthe Monseigneur exerted in poll\ntics.\n\n\nGrand Duke Peter and Princess\nMilitia Nikolajevna are RESPONSE\nbic for the introduction of this\ngentleman with his seances and\napparitions to the Russian court.\n\n\nThe extraordinary power that\nthe Gear Monk\" has gained over\nEmperor Nicholas has just been\nevidenced anew by the fact that,\nwhereas all ecclesiastics were de-\nbarred from being present at the\nlaying of the foundation stone of\nthe new regimental chapel at Ear\naSkOie Selo. two DAYS before the\n\n=== 29_1910-10-28_p1_sn83045433_0010049338A_1910102801_0663.json\nThe Washington herald. · 1910-10-28\ncrops: cached\nheadline: SCARE FAIR GOODS.\n\nNfghtshiFt Parade and Ghost Dance\n\n\nToo Much.\n---\nGalesburg. H.. oct. \"a \"nightshlr:\nparade\" and ghost dance\" which com\npletely terrorized the fair goods Of L,Om-\nbard College. has resulted IN the suspen-\nsion of the five students who were ring\nleaders In the affair\n\n\nThe suspended ones we're members Of\nthe football team. and il Is expected the\nschedule for the remainder Of the season\nwill have 10 be Cancelled.\n\n=== 10_1912-11-22_p10_sn85053089_00294554683_1912112201_0821.json\nThe searchlight. · 1912-11-22\ncrops: cached\nheadline: MAN SEES GHOST IN CELL\n\n\n---\nAllentown. Pa.-Georgs stscker a\nTrenton. who IL serving term In the\nlookup for trying to shoot up the\ntown. for several nights has CON-\nplanned loudly Of 