\tstitute. Mrs Weidel has been doing |\n258\tspecial work with the Speer method\n259\tOf arithmetic and has pleased the Ohio\n260\tteachers immensely\n261\t\n262\t\n263\tThe young women of the Marshall\n264\tCompany surprised Super\n265\tntendent w. G. Bowe at his home, 609\n266\tWest State street, \"Wednesday evening,\n267\t\n268\t=== 54_1885-12-29_pna_sn90059522_00175035357_1885122901_0617.json\n269\tSt. Paul daily globe. [volume] (Saint Paul, Minn.) 1884-1896 · 1885-12-29\n270\tcrops: cached\n271\theadline: GOTHAM SWELLDOM.\n272\t\n273\tNew York Girls and Something Of Their\n274\t\n275\t\n276\tClothes, Shoes and Limps.\n277\t\n278\tThe Vaccination Rage Among the\n279\t\n280\t\n281\tBelles-Opera Fashions.\n282\t\n283\tSpecimen of the New York Swell\n284\t\n285\t\n286\tGotham Glimpses.\n287\t---\n288\tNew York Correspondence:\n289\t\n290\t\n291\tFrom the windows of the Union league\n292\tthe New Yorker may be studied in his or her\n293\tpeculiarities.\n294\t\n295\t\n296\tIi you use the latter pronoun change the\n297\tpeculiarities into idiocies. Not that the\n298\tmale bird is free from features that attract\n299\tyour wondering attention, but that the lady\n300\tbird presents to the strangers eye features\n301\tSO extraordinary and so striking that your\n302\tattention is diverted from her more COM\n303\tmonplace companion.\n304\t\n305\t\n306\tThe men of New York are well worth\n307\tlooking at OF course. The \"doosid\" good\n308\tfellow club man, you know, is always well\n309\tgroomed, lives in bachelor apartments any\n310\twhere from Washington square up to the\n311\tSixty streets, is, above all else, English in\n312\tproclivities and taste, and in his moments\n313\tOF leisure land their name is legion), if it\n314\tdoesn't bore him too much, does the heavy\n315\tagreeable to the fair opponents of social\n316\tart.\n317\t\n318\t\n319\tHe is man, tits true, who doesn't con-\n320\ttribute anything Of Importance toward the\n321\tprogress of the world, but then he fills, and\n322\tfills handsomely, you must admit, niche\n323\tthat would look empty without his pleasing\n324\tform. He is inoffensive, and you are rather\n325\tglad that he is there.\n326\t\n327\t\n328\tThe younger man, the dude. who lives\n329\tbut to become something that he can\n330\tnever be, who is always aping somebody or\n331\tsomething, whose appearance is at times\n332\tgrotesQue, and always contemptible-he\n333\tdeserves but little notice from you. You\n334\tsheer a sheer as he passes, and say short\n335\tmass for the repose of his soul.\n336\t\n337\t\n338\tThese male birds. as l say, catch your\n339\teye as they go by, and you size them up in\n340\ta moment A passing pleasure, as it were,\n341\tand soon forgotten.\n342\t\n343\t\n344\tBut in the notice and study of the female\n345\tspecies, vast fields Of inquiry open out be-\n346\tfore you. Young society girls, young mar\n347\tried women, stout countess dowagers. all\n348\tpresent points of interest that are worth\n349\tprolonged notice and consideration. And\n350\tyet. strange to say, the one most noticeable\n351\tfeature of the younger members Of this\n352\tmore interesting species, is the almost I'M\n353\tqualified and servile imitation of some of\n354\tthe features of the other less interesting\n355\tspecies.\n356\t\n357\t\n358\tTHE NEW YORK GIRL\n359\t\n360\t\n361\tis nothing if not manly. In many of her\n362\thabits, and especially in her dress, she\n363\ttries to look like the men, don't you know.\n364\tRedfern & Overall, and the other ladies'\n365\ttailors, make the clothes for the swell\n366\tyoung woman. Her tailor-made suits cost\n367\ther $125; are fitted by men, and are made\n368\tto look as much like mems clothes as waists\n369\tand skirts can be made to resemble waist\n370\tcoats and trousers.\n371\t\n372\t\n373\tHer shoes are this fall exactly like mems\n374\tshoes. They have thick soles, square box\n375\ttoes, and are made to lace up in front.\n376\tShod with these ''stogies.\" encased like an\n377\tumbrella in a tight-ftting ulster, which fits\n378\tlike paper on the wall over a huge hustle\n379\tprojecting far into the rear; mans hat\n380\ton her head, and a small, big-handled\n381\tumbrella in hand, my lady strides up Fifth\n382\tavenue-one of many, but flying private\n383\tsignals in the way of details of dress, and\n384\tmaking her ''the worst YETI until the next\n385\tone comes along.\n386\t\n387\t\n388\tStrides, however, is hardly the word to\n389\tbe used. She minces, and she makes this\n390\tmincing noticeable by limp. You ask if\n391\tshe is lame. By no means. They all\n392\tlimp, and surely they can't all be lame. 1t\n393\tis simply the fashion to limp. The Princess\n394\tof Wales limps, and for time it was the\n395\tfashion for court ladies to limp also. 1t\n396\tis the swell thing to do here, but for a\n397\tdifferent reason. They have all been vac\n398\tcinated. Not to be vaccinated is not to be\n399\tone Of us girls, and, therefore. whether OF\n400\tno, we limp, l heard a dudish young doc\n401\ttor, the other day at an afternoon tea, say\n402\tthat he had just come from a vaccinating\n403\tseance, where he had just scratched the\n404\tsymmetrical or otherwise calves of some\n405\thalf-dozen society ''girls.\" One Of the\n406\tnumber was actually so timid and modest,\n407\tyou know, that she cut little round hole\n408\tin her stocking, Just large enough for the\n409\tlance rather than to expose to the profess\n410\tsional eye the soft, white eXpanse of her\n411\tshapely leg. That is, 1 dare say it was\n412\tsoft and white, and shapely.\n413\t\n414\t\n415\tNow, these same charming New York\n416\tgirls are guilty of conspicuousness ON the\n417\tstreet. What would you say if you saw a\n418\tsumner come booming up the avenue. a\n419\ttailor-made suit on, and in the way of a\n420\twrap, tight-ftting jacket of bright red\n421\tcloth, military-looking fastenings stretch\n422\ting from one side to the other and involv-\n423\ting a tremendous amount of cord. don't\n424\tknow the scientific name for these fasten-\n425\tings, but they are effective and numerous.\n426\tThe edges of this red, danger-signal sort of\n427\tcoat must be trimmed-that is if you are\n428\tto do the exceedingly swell thing-with\n429\tastrakhan. No, there is no compromise.\n430\tIT MUST BE ASTRAKHAN,\n431\tand of course if you insist, you can put on\n432\tother kinds of fur, such as the vulgar seal\n433\tskin, sable OF otter, but then you will be\n434\twithout the pale of swelldom, and to be\n435\tcorrect, to be dressed unexceptionably, you\n436\tmust have astrakhan and plenty of it. Your\n437\tcoat does not offer space enough for it's dis\n438\tplay. You must also trim the edges of\n439\tyour hat with it. The hat must be of red\n440\tcloth, of small cone shape, and broad\n441\tband of astrakhan around the BASE And\n442\tyou mustn't stop there. If you can't very\n443\twe'll get any more on your dress and coat,\n444\tand you already have muff made of it,\n445\twhy, then have coat made of it for your\n446\tpet dog. He'll look awfully swell in it.\n447\tactually saw that on Madison avenue yes\n448\tterday, hound tottering along under COW\n449\tering of astrakhan.\n450\t\n451\t\n452\twent to the Metropolitan the opening\n453\tnight this season. l didn't expect to be\n454\table to tell what the ladies wore. because\n455\tl knew that not more than from the waist\n456\tupward would be exposed to view from the\n457\tparquette. But 1 was surprised, not to say\n458\tdisappointed.\n459\t\n460\t\n461\tIn the decollete STYLE there were many,\n462\tbut not so many as in previous seasons.\n463\tSquare necks and corsages en- VS. abounded.\n464\tNow, square-neck dress is all right for a\n465\tquiet little dinner, or progressive euchre\n466\tparty, or, say, for church society, but fol\n467\tbox at the opera there is nothing like the\n468\tno-waist dress, commonly called low neck\n469\tand short sleeve. Before the masculine eye\n470\tlooking through acknowledgements, say\n471\tonly moderately-powerful opera glasses, a\n472\tcostume of that kind looms up grandly.\n473\tThe effect is superior. Lines are drawn out\n474\tand soft curves are brought into relief in a\n475\tway that is impossible with the vulgar\n476\thigh-neck dress, whose principal office\n477\tseems to be to hide that which was meant\n478\t\n479\t=== 5_1910-11-27_pna_sn83045462_00280657827_1910112701_0086.json\n480\tEvening star. [volume] (Washington, D.C.) 1854-1972 · 1910-11-27\n481\tcrops: cached\n482\theadline: \n483\t---\n484\t\"But of course you won't\" pursued Miss Payton.\n485\t\"You mustn't! This your life, and it is unworthy.\n486\tDon't let me put any such ideas into your head\n487\t\n488\t\n489\tIl think have learned the value of sound nerves.\n490\the said.\n491\t\n492\t\n493\tMiss Payton reflected. At times he seemed almost\n494\tperson of education.\n495\t\n496\t\n497\tA BRIGHT idea occurred to her. At the mansion\n498\tbungalow of the Payton ranch was certain highly\n499\tornamental stand of rosewood, with many supple\n500\tmentary cylinders resembling black lacquer; silent\n501\tFrom this apparatus the operator could produce at will\n502\tghost voices of very live singers. honeyed melodies\n503\tcaught in maze of little craven lines Why not\n504\tganize party and bring this preserved music to Miles\n505\t\n506\t=== 23_1918-10-19_pna_sn84020438_0051368499A_1918101901_0886.json\n507\tPalisadian. [volume] (Cliffside Park, N.J.) 1906-current · 1918-10-19\n508\tcrops: cached\n509\theadline: White Ghosts-Uqh!\n510\t---\n511\tMany white ghosts appeared in West\n512\tPalisade the past few nights, but they\n513\twere the coverings for plants too\n514\tlarge to bring indoors and out again.\n515\tThe effect was rather startling for\n516\tstrangers.\n517\t\n518\t=== 20_1902-11-05_pna_sn89053684_00414182380_1902110501_0443.json\n519\tThe Savannah morning news. (Savannah, Ga.) 1900-current · 1902-11-05\n520\tcrops: cached\n521\theadline: \n522\t--