7\tAnd Then the Spring Street Fortune Teller\n898\tBlossms Out as Q French Hadame on\n899\t\n900\t\n901\t\n902\t\n903\tWITH A DYING DAUGHTER\n904\t\n905\tAs Mrs. Barron She Summons Spirits\n906\t\n907\t\n908\t...Not of the Liquid Variety\n909\t\n910\tThe Spooks Keep Her and Family 10 High\n911\t\n912\t\n913\tClover for a Time\n914\t\n915\tAnd Then the Spring Street Fortune Teller\n916\tBlossms Out as . French 7adame on\n917\tWall street, Where the Game\n918\t\n919\t\n920\tCoutinues-A Queer Case\n921\t---\n922\tfact that the confirmed criminal, what\n923\tever his specially may be, possesses a\n924\tcertain pride in the neat results of his\n925\tmisdirected genius, just as any man In\n926\tthe more orthodox walks of life, takes\n927\tpride in mastering and carrying into ex-\n928\tecution the varied details of their respec-\n929\ttive avocations.\n930\t\n931\t\n932\tBetween these two classes. however.\n933\tcript fakirs who contrive to keep within\n934\tthe limits of the law, and yet whose\n935\tmethods are essentially criminal, albeit\n936\tthey are not classified as criminals.\n937\tNeedless to say, perhaps, they are even\n938\tmore keenly repudiated by the respecta-\n939\tBILE portion of society.\n940\t\n941\t\n942\tThere has again emerged from her re-\n943\ttirement a lady-for so she proclaims\n944\therself-who belongs to this intermedi-\n945\tate class, who appears to make very\n946\thandsome living by preying upon So\n947\tciety at large. She has husband and\n948\tgrown-up daughter who is quite young\n949\tlady. \"They toll not, neither do they\n950\tspin,\" but while, apparently, they pos\n951\tsess all of the necessaries Of life they\n952\tcontrive also to gain many of the lux\n953\turies made impossible to the hard work\n954\ting mechanic or the average woman\n955\twho works her heart out day by day just\n956\tfor the mere privilege of living.\n957\t\n958\t\n959\tAnd this is made possible by the inge-\n960\tnuity of the mother. She is lady\" of\n961\tmany aliases. She has been known as\n962\tMrs. Orr and Mrs. Barron and then she\n963\trepudiated her country and blossomed\n964\tforth as Nine. but this\n965\tflower of humanity changed it's name,\n966\tthe rankness Of fraud and deception con-\n967\ttinued to be its distinguishing character\n968\tistic.\n969\t\n970\t\n971\tAS Mrs Orr many city residents hav-\n972\ting philanthropic tendencies, contribu-\n973\tted to the support of this united family.\n974\tWith modest and somewhat engaging\n975\tdemeanor Mrs. Orr told how her husband\n976\thad recently died leaving her with\n977\tfamily of small children in totally desti\n978\ttute circumstances. Though not strong\n979\tshe was willing to fight for the little\n980\tones, however, remembering that the\n981\tLord tempers the wind to the shorn\n982\tlamb\" and she was trying to sell few\n983\tarticles, made by herself, in order to\n984\tmake bare living.\n985\t\n986\t\n987\tThe articles in question. bought\n988\twholesale for a nominal sum, sold like\n989\thot cakes and Mrs. Orr (?) must have\n990\tchuckled when she spoke of the \"shorn\n991\tlamb\" She fleeced the folks every time\n992\tthrough working on their sympathies.\n993\t\n994\t\n995\tAt home on San Julian street, not\n996\tlong ago, she rang in a pitiful story of\n997\tyoung daughter wasting away with\n998\tconsumption. With tears in her eyes she\n999\ttold of her fight with poverty since her\n1000\thusbands death and how her daughter\n1001\twas dropping for the comforts and at\n1002\ttention that her condition required. The\n1003\tlady to whom she poured out her woes\n1004\tfound from her that she lived at Six\n1005\tteenth street and Maple avenue and\n1006\tafter buying hei entire stock in trade,\n1007\tgot some of her hearted friends in\n1008\tterested and the same afternoon loaded\n1009\tup buggy with good things for the\n1010\tdying daughter, as well as the mother,\n1011\tand drove out to the address given. The\n1012\timposition was then discovered for the\n1013\taddress was a fake\" one.\n1014\t\n1015\t\n1016\tThe Associated Charities had been\n1017\tworked at an early stage of the game\n1018\tbut Mrs. Orr, to use her most common\n1019\tcognomen, had been so skillful in ex\n1020\ttorting sympathy from people, at so\n1021\tmany dollars per head, that the police\n1022\tbegan to investigate. Chief Glass re-\n1023\tports her as being one of the very clev-\n1024\tcrest of those fakirs who work daringly\n1025\talong the danger line without actually\n1026\tinfringing upon it.\n1027\t\n1028\t\n1029\tScenting the presence of the police\n1030\tMrs. Orr developed into Mrs. Barron and\n1031\ttook rooms on South Spring street,\n1032\twhere a bright band of spirits also took\n1033\tup their abode and assisted her in telling\n1034\t| fortunes. Fortunes were read off with\n1035\tall the ease of creased lightning at 81\n1036\tper head for gentlemen, half price for\n1037\tladies' For a time the spiritualistic\n1038\t! dodge worked to a charm but recently\n1039\t| Mrs. Barron saw fit to skip out from her\n1040\t| Spring street habitation, it being under\n1041\t| stood she was going to make the grand\n1042\t| tour\" that spiritual mediums frequent\n1043\t| ly make, for the purpose of giving other\n1044\t| cities the benefit of the band of spirits\n1045\t| surrounding her.\n1046\t\n1047\t\n1048\tThe grand tour\" really meant the\n1049\t! blossoming forth on Wall street as\n1050\tMadame So and So, where she has con-\n1051\t\n1052\t\n1053\ttinued to pump spiritual thunder at sc\n1054\tcents and 81 per clap.\n1055\t\n1056\t\n1057\tBut spiritualistic mediums, In COM\n1058\tmon with other businesses, fake and\n1059\totherwise, have found the financial\n1060\t! grass growing rather short. Madame\n1061\t! has therefore again taken to the high\n1062\t| way and is holding up soft-hearted\n1063\tmothers having children of their own\n1064\t| at the point of a well sharpened tongue\n1065\t| and basketful of trumpery articles\n1066\t| Complaints are beginning to come into\n1067\t\n1068\t\n1069\tthe office of the Associated Charities, as\n1070\t| we'll as the police, and it may be well for\n1071\tmadame to again take to the fortune\n1072\t! telling business. 1t, too, is a fraud but\n1073\tnot in all cases illegal, albeit 1t IS diff\n1074\t! cult to separate the sheep from the\n1075\tgoats.\n1076\t\n1077\t\n1078\tAS for the ordinary householder II\n1079\t\n1080\t\n1081\tmay, perhaps, be well If he or she, as the\n1082\t\n1083\t\n1084\tcase NAV be- will think a long time be-\n1085\t\n1086\t=== 3_1896-07-08_pna_sn84026907_00295862373_1896070801_0058.json\n1087\tThe Lexington dispatch. [volume] (Lexington, South Carolina) 1870-1917 · 1896-07-08\n1088\tcrops: cached\n1089\theadline: OBITUARY.\n1090\t---\n1091\tGeorge Violet, infant daughter OF\n1092\tGeorge A.*nlAgaes R. Hal:iwanger.\n1093\twas born on the 22d day OF Sept.\n1094\t1895, and died June 9th, 1896,\n1095\taged nine mouths and five days.\n1096\tOnly few months ago, her father\n1097\tpreceded her to the spirit land and\n1098\tonly q mother snl wife with one\n1099\tlittle girl is left Of the once charmed\n1100\tfamily circle. A bud plucked from\n1101\tearth to bloom in heaven. We gently\n1102\tlaid her to rest in the cemetery OF\n1103\tCaper's Chapel, by the side of her\n1104\tfather. IS,\n1105\t\n1106\t=== 24_1945-06-25_p1_sn83045462_00280604549_1945062501_0589.json\n1107\tEvening star. · 1945-06-25\n1108\tcrops: cached\n1109\theadline: Charles Town Results\n1110\t---\n1111\tFIRST RACE-Purse. 5000: 3-year-oldi\n1112\tand up; claiming; about q 4k furlongs\n1113\tHutoka fEdensb $50 32O go\n1114\tTen Oaks (Grant) 42O 3S0\n1115\tTime Burner (BakhSh) 4S}0\n1116\tTime, 0:50A.\n1117\t\n1118\t\n1119\t: Also ran--Jo Beth Bum. Over Gold\n1120\tBonnie Ina, Morbrook, Dunemall.\n1121\t\n1122\t\n1123\tSECOND RACE-Purse, 5000: 3-year.\n1124\tolds and up; allowances; about Az fur\n1125\tlongs.\n1126\tFlying West tCarillo) 1920 $50 400\n1127\tPatty Boy fEdens) 44O 400\n1128\tBig