ies of South America,\n1621\twhen Venezuela and New Grenada (the\n1622\t| latter then included the Isthmus) united\n1623\tin establishing one central government\n1624\t| for the purpose of resisting Spain. Ten\n1625\twears later Venezuela retired from this\n1626\tunion and constituted herself a sep\n1627\tcrate republic. After the resigna-\n1628\tton of Bolivia (1S30) she again\n1629\tJoined herself to New Grenada; but the\n1630\tunion lasted only few months. In\n1631\tNovember, 1881, another separation\n1632\ttook place, and at the same time it was\n1633\tdecided that the former province of\n1634\tQuito should constitute q separate\n1635\tgovernment, under the name of Ecua\n1636\tdor, thus dividing the former unwieldy\n1637\t\"Co!ombia\" into three distinct and In\n1638\tdependent republics, viz: Venezuela,\n1639\tEcuador and New Granada.\n1640\t\n1641\t\n1642\tANOTHER CHANGE.\n1643\t\n1644\t\n1645\tIn 1861 another radical change oc.\n1646\tCured, since which date the United\n1647\tStates of Colombia\" has been the\n1648\tofficial title Of what was before known\n1649\tas New Granada. Its government\n1650\textends extraordin&gy inducements to\n1651\tforeigners and especially to citizens OF\n1652\tthe North American republics, to per-\n1653\tsuade them to make homes here.\n1654\tGrants of some OF the finest and on the\n1655\tface ofR the earth are offered for their\n1656\tacceptance free of cost, providing only\n1657\tthat they ayow an intention to settle\n1658\tpermanently in Colombia.\n1659\t\n1660\t\n1661\tNew Granada, with its skies of\n1662\tcloudless blue, its luscious fruits ana\n1663\tbeautiful flowers, its picturesque val\n1664\tley and the grandeur Of It's mountains,\n1665\tsottened by eternsl summer, would De\n1666\tfor the emigrant one OF the most de-\n1667\tsirable places on the globe-the ultima\n1668\tthule of his desires-Were it not for The\n1669\tchina e influences. The unhealthy IA\n1670\tture of the coast presents an obstacle\n1671\tformidable, if not unS9rmOunGable, to\n1672\tcolonization by the northern races.\n1673\tEspecially on the Pacific side. the whole\n1674\tcountry is a network Of muddy creeks\n1675\tand sWampy islands, worse, if possible,\n1676\tthan the western shores of Africa.\n1677\tThere are nitric valleys healthy a\n1678\tany in the world, and p ateous and ex-\n1679\ttensive tracts half way up the noun\n1680\ttain sides where Paradise might be\n1681\tlooated-bUt hemming them in IS the\n1682\tfever-haunted coast.\n1683\t\n1684\t\n1685\tTHE RATIONAL DEBT.\n1686\t\n1687\t\n1688\tColomLia's inde btedness to England\n1689\talone is over $4,000 900, and there is\n1690\tnot the slightest prospect Of its ever\n1691\tbeing paid Since the emancipation of\n1692\ttheir slaves, in 1852, labor cannot be\n1693\tcontrolled in any way, not even by\n1694\tmoney-fOr why should man exert\n1695\thimself when he has no ambition to\n1696\tcrafty, no aspirations to attain and 70\n1697\tneeds to suppiy2 In a land where the\n1698\tbanana and the black man flourish side\n1699\tby SIDE, both without effort Or aultiva-\n1700\tton. is no congenial place for Anglo\n1701\tSaxons.\n1702\t\n1703\t\n1704\tNature having provided so bounti-\n1705\tfully in these parts for almost every\n1706\twant OF mar, the ignorant nali7es are\n1707\twholly without energy, thrift or enter\n1708\tprise, With them every thing is DIananG\n1709\tthe tomorrow\" thai never comes.\n1710\tThey live with no thought or care for\n1711\tthe future, the \"eVen teaor\" of their\n1712\tsouls disturbed By neither doubts nor\n1713\tfears, nor vsulting ambitions; and\n1714\tbeing devout Catholics every one. even\n1715\tdeath has for them'no terrors, but they\n1716\tare quite ready to shuttle off this NOR\n1717\ttai coil at any moment, as indiferently\n1718\tas they have lived.\n1719\t\n1720\t\n1721\tCOMMENTED PEOPLE.\n1722\t\n1723\t\n1724\tSo strongly marked are the lines of\n1725\tcaste, and so impossible the gulf be-\n1726\ttween the few partisans and the many