fevers, its\n1769\tdistorting glass-both drawn forth from dark\n1770\tcorners the fears Of defenceess childhood,\n1771\twhich press and cut with iron fangs into\n1772\tthe PROSTATE soul. The fair scenes of dreams\n1773\tmostly play on an after-stage, whereas the\n1774\tfrightful ones choose for theirs the cradle and\n1775\tthe nursery. Moreover, in fever, the ice\n1776\thands Of the fear of ghosts, the striking one\n1777\tof the teachers and parents, and every claw\n1778\twith which fate has passed the young heart,\n1779\tthemselves out to catch the wandering man.\n1780\tParents, consider then that every childhoo's\n1781\tRupert--the name given in Germany to the\n1782\t\n1783\t\n1784\tfictitious being employed to frighten children\n1785\tinto obedience-ev though it has lain chained\n1786\tfor tens of years, yet breaks loose and gains\n1787\tmastery over the man so soon as it finds him\n1788\ton sick-bed. The first fright is more dan\n1789\tgerous the sooner it happens; as the man\n1790\tgrows older, he is less easily frightened; the\n1791\tlittle cradle Of the child is more easily quite\n1792\tdarkened than the starry heaven of the man.\n1793\t\n1794\t=== 52_1919-10-31_p9_sn83045433_0028076405A_1919103101_0491.json\n1795\tThe Washington herald. · 1919-10-31\n1796\tcrops: cached\n1797\theadline: SPIRITUALISTS.\n1798\t\n1799\tWashing;on's Favorite Adviser\n1800\tPROF. MARCUS La MAR\n1801\t---\n1802\tMost remarkable reader Of human destiny OF\n1803\tthe present. age. tells your name In full also full\n1804\tnames Of husband wife Or sweetheart; reveals\n1805\tyour tnnermost secrets. helps you to gain your\n1806\tevery desire; brings about marriage with the Que\n1807\tyou love. and gives never failing help and ad-\n1808\tvice on business. law suits or any affair Of life.\n1809\tCall today; he will surprise YOU -\n1810\t"}]},"uuid":"64cbf6e9-3a48-4112-9ade-edaed2dba594","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:00:25.463Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/