 pi-\n475\tano, is positive that the war will end\n476\tin January, 1919.\n477\t\n478\t\n479\tThe Ouija informed its owner that\n480\tthe world would be less sinful after\n481\tpeace had been declared and that the\n482\tpeople would live happily ever after.\n483\t\n484\t\n485\tWhile it declined to say what dis\n486\tposition would be made of the Euro\n487\tpean monarchs, it did say that the ski\n488\tdoc sign would be hung on all of them\n489\tand that Europe would not only be-\n490\tcome safe for Democracy but every\n491\tnation would be a republic. When\n492\tasked. whether the report that Car\n493\tNicholas has been made king of ST.\n494\tIBERIA was true, the Ouija promptly re-\n495\tpied IN the negative. 1t said Nick\n496\tcouldn't come back.\n497\t\n498\t\n499\tThe war Will not be any worse than\n500\t1t is today, according to Ouija, the\n501\tspirits apparently believing that the\n502\tlimit has been reached. When the\n503\tOuiJa board told Mr.. Schmittzehe that\n504\tCol. I. Roosevelt would not be Presi-\n505\tdent again, Schmittzehe simply re-\n506\tmarked: \"Ain't it the truth\" and\n507\toulJa was pronounced a thoroughly\n508\tboard and then placed back\n509\tIN the showcase. \"Them spirits are\n510\tnot as dead as you think\" added\n511\tSchmittzehe.\n512\t\n513\t=== 2_1912-05-06_p1_sn93055779_00295872664_1912050601_0909.json\n514\tThe Cairo bulletin. · 1912-05-06\n515\tcrops: cached\n516\theadline: NEVER AGAIN FOR THIS MAN\n517\t\n518\tYouth Meant Well, but Recollection\n519\tOf Episode Is Haunting\n520\t\n521\t\n522\tMemory.\n523\t---\n524\tThe newly established practice In\n525\tthe Equal Rights association Of APP\n526\tpointing attractive young women to\n527\tdispose of suffrage literature, badges,\n528\tsandwiches, etc, has been the cause of\n529\tsome amusing mistakes. One Of these\n530\twas wholly lacking in humor, from the\n531\tpoint of view of the unfortunate per.\n532\tson who lived through 1t.\n533\t\n534\t\n535\tIt was this way: An amiable young\n536\tman. walking down Broadway one\n537\tmorning q short time ago, saw stand\n538\ting on the corner q beautiful young\n539\tgirl She held In her hand bunch Of\n540\tviolets and camelias. At her feet lay\n541\ttray Of these flowers, and she\n542\tglanced shyly and appealingly at the\n543\tpassers-by. The young man had\n544\tstarted across the street when he saw\n545\ther. He hesitated, turned, looked\n546\tback at her uncertainty, and then\n547\tsquaring his Shoulders, strobe to her\n548\tside. 3 ~\n549\t\n550\t\n551\tMay be permitted to buy them an\n552\tand help the cause along?\" he asked\n553\tCALAMITY, standing before her, hat m\n554\thand, and smiling an irresistible\n555\tsmilr. ..M...\n556\t\n557\t\n558\tTie girl turned, looked at him for\n559\tan instant In blank amazement, and\n560\tthen flushed Indignantly, The wretch.\n561\ted youth suddenly saw a boy dart\n562\tfrom nearby store and rush up to\n563\tthe young lady with a handful OF\n564\tchange. She took the change, pinned\n565\ton her flowers and with whitening\n566\tglance at the would-be supporter OF\n567\tthe cause who remained rooted to\n568\tthe spot, marched away.\n569\t\n570\t\n571\tWhen ho was able to speak dispas.\n572\tsionatcly Of the incident, the youth de-\n573\tclared that to the best of his recollec-\n574\tton the pavement opened and swal.\n575\t\n576\t=== 10_1911-11-10_pna_sn85042344_00237284501_1911111001_0683.json\n577\tTulsa daily world. [volume] (Tulsa, Indian Territory [Okla.]) 1905-1919 · 1911-11-10\n578\tcrops: cached\n579\theadline: Federal ACTION\n580\t\n581\t\n582\tRAISES VALUES\n583\t\n584\tADDITIONAL TERRITORY PLACED\n585\tABOVE UARANTlNE MEANS\n586\t\n587\t\n588\t$500 \\ HEAD.\n589\t\n590\tTICK ABOUT ERAOICTED\n591\t\n592\tProclamation Affect, haOut 10000\n593\tCattle Now Taucuing for Market.\n594\t\n595\t\n596\tstate Board Also to Act\n597\t---\n598\tover two thousand heed ~ Catt'e\n599\tare now being fsl at point just north\n600\tOf the northern boundary line Of the