o bring the informa-\n297\tton. He succeeded In gaining what\n298\the wanted and. dressing himself In a\n299\tfantastic costume, started forth on foot\n300\tfor the city.\n301\t\n302\t\n303\twalking along road with no other\n304\tweapon than light cane, he met a\n305\tparty of Chinese Boxers Since Hig-\n306\tgins was coming from the direction OF\n307\ttheir enemies the Cinnamon were dis\n308\tposed to chop him up at once. but\n309\tthey couldn't understand his queer\n310\tcostume There is not more super\n311\tHtitious race in the world than the\n312\tChinese unless 1t Is certain low grade\n313\tMohammedans. As the Boxers APP\n314\tproached Higgins, seeing him come\n315\tright along without fear, their courage\n316\tbegan to ooze out at their finger end\n317\tThey stopped and waited for him to\n318\tcome up. Higgins tossed a little\n319\tsphere as big as a marble among them.\n320\twhich exploded. and. though 1t did no\n321\tharm, it scattered them. They turn\n322\ted and saw the stranger marching on\n323\tsilently like a specter. He raised his\n324\that, and every hair on his head stood\n325\tstraight up. That took what courage\n326\tthere was in them, and he saw them\n327\tno more.\n328\t\n329\t\n330\tThe next lot Of Boxers he met were\n331\tholder. They blocked the road and\n332\tcried out something in Chinese which\n333\tHiggins didn't understand. Higgins\n334\tstopped One Of the Cinnamon advanc-\n335\ted, while the others skunk back. When\n336\the got within a few yards of the\n337\tstrange apparition 1t drew an imagi-\n338\tnary circle of fire about it with the\n339\tend OF its cane.\n340\t\n341\t\n342\tThe advancing man retreated on his\n343\tsupports.\n344\t\n345\t\n346\tOne OF the Boxers now brought gun\n347\tto his shoulder and fired at Higgins.\n348\t1t was a close call for the soldier. for\n349\tthe bullet whistled within an inch Of\n350\this ear. Had not the Boxer who fred\n351\tbeen affected by superstition he would\n352\tprobably have killed his man Higgins\n353\tdidn't lose his presence OF mind. but\n354\tturned the incident to his advantage.\n355\tHe stood with his lips parted and\n356\tdrawn so that bis enemies could see |\n357\tthe ball they had fred held between |\n358\this teeth. Then. taking 1t in his hand. /\n359\the threw II among them. Had be |\n360\tthrown q hand grenade he couldn't !\n361\thave scattered them more efrectualiy. !\n362\t\n363\t\n364\tHiggins was now getting near the\n365\twalls Of the city and began TO use his |\n366\teyes. He also made notes and draw\n367\tings. He had a pocket glass with him /\n368\tand found IL valuable. While he was\n369\tgazing a party Of Chinese horsemen\n370\tswent down on him. Though puzzled\n371\t\n372\t=== 1_1920-05-13_pna_sn78000873_00279525036_1920051301_0165.json\n373\tThe Republican journal. [volume] (Belfast, Me.) 1829-current · 1920-05-13\n374\tcrops: cached\n375\theadline: CASTORIA\n376\t\n377\t\n378\tFor Infants and Children\n379\t\n380\t\n381\tIn Use For Over 30YearS\n382\tz,rs III s. Of 1sf4zzSzzs<\n383\t\n384\tConvention of Maine Spiritualists\n385\t---\n386\tThe Gath annual convention of the Maine\n387\tState Spiritualist Association will be held\n388\tin Guilford, Maine, on May 18th and 10th.\n389\t\n390\t\n391\tThe night before will be devoted to\n392\treception and general conference. All day\n393\tSaturday will be taken up with The bust\n394\tness sessions. On Saturday evening, Sun\n395\tday afternoon and Sunday evening there\n396\twill be public lectures and seances con-\n397\tQuoted by Maud Litch Torrey of Lynn,\n398\tMass, one of New Eng lands most dis\n399\ttinguished lecturers and psychics.\n400\t\n401\t\n402\tSunday morning will be given up to\n403\tgeneral conference in which prominent\n404\tSpiritualists from various sections of the\n405\tState will take part, discussing those\n406\tthemes and problems connected with the\n407\tadvancement of the science, philosophy\n408\tand religion of Spiritualism in Maine\n409\tThis convention bids fair to be one of\n410\tthe most important in recent years as\n411\tthe activities of the State Association\n412\tduring the coming year will necessarily\n413\tincrease in order to keep pace with the\n414\trapidly growing interest in psychic mat\n415\ttiers on the part of the general public.\n416\tThe State Association has received sever\n417\tal requests of substantial amounts during\n418\tthe past year, and the Endowment Fund\n419\tis rapidly assuming proportions where it\n420\twill be possible to carry out some of the\n421\tlong cherished plans which have been\n422\tcrippled for many years by the lack of\n423\tfunds.\n424\t\n425\t=== 29_1904-02-29_p4_sn84020358_00271744432_1904022901_0448.json\n426\tThe daily morning journal and courier. · 1904-02-29\n427\tcrops: cached\n428\theadline: \n429\t---\n430\tDr. Marcus E. Peterson of Brooklyn had a hurry call the other night, and took short cut across an old cemetery to save time. He fell head foremost into an empty grave, and might have died from exposure but for his dog, which jumped into the grave and licked his masters face and shook him till he revived him. The people of the neigh borhood think the cemetery is haunted, and number of people returning from a social affair and who, hearing the dog howl, looked over the fence, thought they had certainly surprised a ghost when they saw a form rise out of the grave and walk across the lot followed by the dog.\n431\t\n432\t=== 38_1954-10-02_p1_sn83045462_00280607319_1954100201_0078.json\n433\tEvening star. [volume] (Washington, D.C.) 1854-1972 · 1954-10-02\n434\tcrops: cached\n435\theadline: London Arms Accord Reported;\n436\tGruenther Sees Reds Defeat\n437\tEventually if War Should Come\n438\t\n439\tControl Formula\n440\tFound in TuIks,\n441\tSpook Says\n442\t\n443\t\n444\tBULLETIN\n445\t\n446\tBULLETIN\n447\t---\n448\tLONDON (R.-French Pre-\n449\tmier Pierre Mendes-France\n450\twalked out Of the nine-power\n451\tconference on rearming Ger\n452\tmany today saying he was i