tern yarn spinners\nfor the lifeboats and incidental tenders.\n\n\n\"Do / know any sea yarns?\" commented\none ardent seeker for the new job. Are\nthere any don't know? Forty eight years,\nservice. fore and aft seen on the high\nseas and what | don't know aint. Not\nmeanin' TO boast. you understand, hut just\nStain plain facts, | kin hold my head up in\nany old aggregation of marines you want\nto get together.\n\n\nII run away to sea when / just a\nkid. took my knocks till they made man OF\nme- and went up the ladder till I come TO\nport as first mate of the finest sain' vessel\never shipped out OF san Francisco Bay.\nThat's my record. And perhaps / haven't\npicked up yarn or two ia that time. DIE\never hear the one about the girl and the\nequator? or the one about the iceberg and\nthe ghost ship Tyrant H.? Say, / know a\nlot more, too.\n\n\nPut me I'm the emokin' room and III\nguarantee TO break up all the poker and\npinochle games In sight. Set me down I'm\nthe main saloon and there won't be no ladies\nknittln' or writin' homeslck letters back TO\nthe folks on shore. Give me the kids for an\n\n=== 4_1920-06-30_pna_sn88056159_00295868107_1920063001_0139.json\nThe Challis messenger. (Challis, Idaho) 1912-current · 1920-06-30\ncrops: cached\nheadline: RIVAL MANAGERS\n\n\nHUSTLE FOR VOTES\n\nPRE-coNvENTloN SITUATION At\nSAN FRANCISCO ONE OF\n\n\nSKIES AND SEvENS.\n\nBoosters For Half z Dozen Asplrants\nFor Coveted Nomination Active\nAmong Uninstrueted 0eieoates-\n\n\nMeAdoo Boom viii Not Down.\n---\nSan FranciscO.-The pre-cOnventi0n\nsituation seems to be one Of skies and\nsevens. More and more elements Of\nuncertainty appear In the lineup Of the\nDemocratic national convention as the\nleaders of first magnitude arrive in\nincreasing numbers and put their\nheads together over questions Of poll\ncies and men.\n\n\nFor time the platform held its\nplace as the big topic Of cOgitatiOn and\nnegotiation, with the problem Of bone\ndry prohibition the chief material for\ncontroversy.\n\n\nTalk Of candidates, in a mOribund\nstage for week, was revived appre-\nGladly as the convention crowds\ngathered. Boosters for Palmer, Cox\nand half dozen other aspirants be-\ncame increasingly active among I'M\ninstructed delegates, and a whole bevy\nOF favOrite sons and dark horses\nbl0ssomed out with headquarters of\ntheir own.\n\n\nMeantime the phantom McAdOo\nboom stalked serenely through hotel\ncorridors and conference rooms, leav-\ning behind trail of uncertainty and\nspeculation. Though publicly execut-\ned ut the hands of Mr.. McAdOO him\nself, the movement will not down.\nIndeed, its perambulations are sug-\ngestipe Of the pink of vigOr, and Ut\nturned up unlimited as the ghost at\nthe council table of more than one\ncandidates manager.\n\n\nOn several questions Of convention\norganization, too. the party chiefs\nhave been in a quandary. There were\nsome rumblings of fight against\nSenator Glass, the administration\nchoice for chairman Of the platform\ncommittee. and the problem of choos-\ning a permanent convention chairman\ngot into mess which threatened to\nupset seriously the plans of some adj\nministration supporters.\n\n\nSenator Walsh of Montana, who\nvoted in the senate last March for\nratification Of the peace treaty with\nthe Republican reservations, promises\nto become the storm center of the or\nganization fight. In some quarters he\nwas urged as a candidate against\nSenator Glass for head of the platform\nthough others thought he\nshould have the permanent chairman\nship instead. He had the backing of\nWilliam Jennings Bryan and was\nsaid to be favored also by other\npowerful forces more or less out Of\naccord with some administration\npolicies.\n\n\nSenator Glass, who arrived Thurs\nday from Washington as the COM\nmonty reputed spokesman of the\nWhite House, denied that the presi-\ndent would seek to control the de-\nalterations here. The senator came to\nmake fight favorable to the admins\ntration, but If he brought any word of\nWhite House preference between can\nit did not show up on the sur\nface in the conferences.\n","numLines":1565,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1565}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"42a462c7-61cb-4a48-a648-a3d4a2585875","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
