63\tII they rode on the moon thro' the boundless\n1264\tblue,\n1265\t\n1266\t\n1267\tThey would Join my chorus-tu-whit tu.whoo\n1268\tThey would alter their notions Of virtue and\n1269\tsin,\n1270\t\n1271\t\n1272\tAnd weigh against their world the head Of q\n1273\t| nm!\n1274\t\n1275\t=== 9_1938-09-22_pna_sn87075008_00340580047_1938092201_0879.json\n1276\tMorgan County Democrat. (McConnelsville, Ohio) 1886-1943 · 1938-09-22\n1277\tcrops: cached\n1278\theadline: Worshipping The One God\n1279\t---\n1280\tCoadaism is a combination relig\n1281\ton, including in it's worship not only\n1282\tBuddah, CONTIGUOUS, Laotse, but al\n1283\tSO Christ. Its leaders have taken\n1284\tquotations from many religious\n1285\tbooks, including the Bible, to make\n1286\tup their liturgy, and there is a spir-\n1287\titistic element in their cult They\n1288\tuse of ouija board. Pictures of the\n1289\tEye, the symbol of the Great Intel\n1290\tligence, are sold to thousands for\n1291\tthirty-five cents, and are worshipped\n1292\tin the homes. 1t is religion of an\n1293\tcestor worship, of ritual and robes,\n1294\ta formidable cult of 100000 people\n1295\tin Cochin, China, and an enemy and\n1296\tcompetitor Of Christian teaching.\n1297\t\n1298\t\n1299\tIn Turkey one of the higher Gov\n1300\ternment Schools has requested from\n1301\tthe Bible Society a small grant Of\n1302\tBibles for it's English Department\n1303\tTogether with these the Society in\n1304\tcluded copy of the Revised Turkish\n1305\tNew Testament. Later it was dis\n1306\tcovered that since it was put on the\n1307\tlibrary shelves, this New Testament\n1308\thas been in almost constant circula-\n1309\tton among the students, and that\n1310\tthere was small waiting list OF\n1311\tthose who had signed for the Book\n1312\ton its return.\n1313\t"}]},"uuid":"67535dc0-b436-4a8e-a689-75505a73e8da","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:06:26.333Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/c1/g15.txt","content":"=== 27_1881-05-28_pna_sn84022553_00202197255_1881052801_0048.json\nBradford opinion. [volume] (Bradford, Vt.) 1874-1881 · 1881-05-28\ncrops: cached\nheadline: \n---\nRev. Waite did not give his ex-\npose of spiritualism as announced\nlast Friday evening. He conclud-\ned that he could not Wait for an\naudience, and SO he started for\nEly.\n\n=== 19_1906-06-15_pna_sn88076515_00295863936_1906061501_0777.json\nDevils Lake inter-ocean and Devils Lake free press. (Devils Lake, Ramsey County, N.D.) 1905-1909 · 1906-06-15\ncrops: cached\nheadline: SUFFER J /. |: FOR OPIUM.\n\nSAN FRANCISCO FIRE CON\n\n\nsUMED ALL SUPPLIES.\n\nUsers Of the Drug to the Number Of\n10000 Deprived Of It and\nMany Rave for Their\n\n\nI'D n stDope.'\n---\nSan Francisco. of the abundance\nOF supplies which have been sent here\nsince the calamity OF few weeks ago\nnothing has been more heartily wei\ncoined than the quantity, small though\nit be, Of that brown, gummy substance,\nthe dope fiend's', key to paradise, the\nabsence Of which during the period Of\ndevastation and turmoil is responsible\nfor many cases OF insanity, temporary\nand permanent. 3 &\n\n\nThe opium fiend needed but little the\nlack of food, water and shelter, but\nthe want of his dope\" actually drove\nhim crazy. None but those who have\nbecome a prey to this drug can realize\nwhat it means to go without it for\n\"a hours, two days, a week, and in\nsome cases even longer. A living hell\nwas theirs while they hunted from\nplace to place besieging the few re-\nnaming drug stores Of San Francisco.\nscampering 10 Oakland, where the ar\nticle was equally scarce and eventually\nbecoming insane when their craving\ncould not be satisfied.\n\n\nAnd such prices! Here, where more\nof the drug is consumed than in any\nother four large cities Of the country\ncombined and where it was almost as\ncommon and marketable as the ordi-\nnary articles Of diet, the diminished\nsupply pushed the price up to $40 a\nshell. and almost impossible to get at\nthat. Those searching for relief from\nthe pangs Of the fiendish habit gave\nthe authorities nearly as much trouble\nas the starving men, women and chill\n\n\ndren who were piteously crying for\nbread\n\n\nSpokane and Seattle soon came to\nthe relief of the pillmakers and rushed\nin the hop by. the hogshead. but even\nthen the supply was far below normal.\n\n\nOnly those who know San Francisco\ncan imagine the situation. Nearly all\nthe opium-smoking ..joints\" were in\nChinatown, yet the real swell pipe.\nhitters\" had their dreams in other sec\nlions of the city. Every house in\nChinatown could muster full quota\nof t.dope\" fends, to say nothing OF the\nvisitors who came along regularly for\ntheir little seance. These conditions\nnaturally would make Chinatown the\ncenter of the industry, and it was here\nthat most Of the stuff was stored in\nadequate quantities. .$ I'D X; Il\n\n\nThe fire soon annihilated Chinatown\nThe WoeSsn shacks went down before\n\"a Ao mo {, g VIII oat boPoras +bo ,ox,tpt,\nand when the fire had spent its fury\nthe smold ering embers and filthy de-\nbris choked up the streets, the tunnels,\nsubways, dugouts and underground\npassages for which this section was\nnoted. These burrows contained most\nOf the city's supply Of the opium, and\nwhile there may be some Of the drug\nthat survived the flames, it has not yet\nbeen brought to the surface.\n\n\nThe HOP sharks were noticeable\nall over San Francisco before the first\nday of the conHagration had passed.\nThey could be singled out running\nabout in wild frenzy, begging at the\nfew remaining drug stores for relief.\nThey numbered fully $1,000, white and\n4 r g t.\nyellow. h. N\n\n\nThe day after the fire started these\nsufferers added thousandfold to the\ndifficulties Of the authorities and Oak\nland soon became the center of their\nsiege. There was no relief in that\nquarter and by the morning Of the sec\nond day the fiends literally stormed\nthe drug stores. with little result.\n\n\nThe soldiers, vigiiant at all times,\nwould corral these morbid creatures,\nand when they became temporarily in\nsane would turn them loose. The sto-\nries which travelled east that many\npeople were crazed by the excitement\nand horror were in some cases nothing\nmore than instances Of the \"pipe hit\nters' rawlings. t 5s58\n\n=== 2_1930-03-08_p1_sn83045499_00514159567_1930030801_0461.json\nThe Daily Alaska empire. · 1930-03-08\ncrops: cached\nheadline: OUIJA BOARD\n\n SPELLED OUT\n\n WORD 'AvENCE'\n\nTribal Superstition Is Also Given as Cause for\n\n Buffalo Murder\n---\nBUFFALO, New York, March 8. Two Indian women are in jail charged with the murder of Mrs. Clothilde Marchand, wife of the famous artist Henry Marchand, Curator of the Buffalo Museum of Science. after one of the women, Lillian Jimer5on confessed she used an ouija board and also tribal su- perstitions which melted Mrs. Man. cy Bowen, aged 6 years, to kill the artists wife.\n\n Unrequited love for the artist, is blamed for the killing, Miss Jimer- son said. She is 35 years of age, whom Marchand used as model. She became infatuated with him.\n\n Miss Jimerson said she told the older Indian woman that messages from her husband, in the spirit land, cried out to avenge. Then the cuija board did the same thing as well as. spelling out instructions to go to the Marchand home and kill the woman. The woman did go. She struck Mrs. Marchand with a hammer over the head, then thrust a wad of paper and chloro- form down her throat.\n\n=== 13_1942-02-14_p1_sn93062828_00332899478_1942021401_0066.json\nThe Omaha guide. · 1942-02-14\ncrops: cached\nheadline: AT THE DANCE FEB. 9th\n---\nAT THE DANCE FEB. 9th\n\n\nEdgar Alord pulling a snake\nwith Cert Yancey.\"\n\n\nEdith Cottrell Seen having a gay\ntime with Cowboy. Say, Cottrell\nis he still your ideal?\n\n\nElwood left Joyce at home.\n\n\nWe saw Juanita Wynn and\nPreacher. (They were pretty well\nwrapped up there.) Congratulate\nions to the newly weds, Vineta\nSwancey and Pauncho.\n\n\nEloise seemed to be killing her\nself with Herman Franklin. Does\nnot she realize the little Jasper\nBaby's feeling will be deeply hurt\n-. and we mean deeply.\nMack Franklin with this noJ-so\nbad-too-look at Chick from Texas,\nCrying to knock your broth.r\nout p\n\n\nPrice Terrell Jr., was seen with\nMiss Frampton after the dance al\nso Billy Richardson with Edith.\nGoing Back Home.)\n\n=== 14_1913-02-20_p1_sn83045652_0028077845A_1913022001_0658.json\nTaÌˆgliche Omaha tribuÌˆne. [volume] (Omaha, Nebr.) 1912-1926 · 1913-02-20\ncrops: faro_1913/1913-02-20_p1_sn83045652_0028077845A_1913022001_0658.json: the article's words aren't in its boxes\nheadline: \n---\nHaunt trdgsn6 duf Gilas.\n\n\nOr III es!\" oadts bieIsr. .Ntnl\naud Der Shnurrbart ieblt uno Iei\nrsn gsipesurgtu bas p.oantiId @eI\nme Isut = bic auesn finb oisi.fbsn\nSect bssreife Id tpobl, oaB Id Ms,\nTito grantoip unre6t tat, als Id ibl\nidrisb. iis miiHe ii6 setduidt bdbtn\naihter Tel tot. Gr lsbt! Sier feb\nu ia ltib9aftig bot mit!\"\n\n\nl~nipiQtiirlid mar tr tuie Elm,\nMauer Dor Den gsiben fieben aebli.l\nben uHo DerbiHosrt. ie baour9 an\nWeit,rgeben.\n\n\ngWHniheu Gle ,tipas bon mir,\nmsin Gerr2\" frusts Der gssleiter be,\nDame nun bofIi6 iaHft.\n\n\nDie Stimme mar ptidtr aIs Die,\niDslde 5smpel bon Dem @erbSr in\noer @rinneruna bate.\n\n\naber ods beirrte ibn ni6t, Der\nbenz dHoern 1ur itarr in Die 4uaen\nblidte. 4les tonnte man perGnoern\n- aber oisie nidt!\n\n\nSic iparsn es! Gle iuoren es Be-\nfimmtl\n\n\nga, fdgte er nun, i'd m0Gte\nGle um cine unierreoung bitten, Serr\n0r. Ritter. Sc bunosIt ii4 INN\na%uftl1rungen =\"\n\n\ngu benen i9 natiirlid nit @:rs\nanigen bersit pdre, tpenu i4. . /.\nRiater biebel Dies lit nitt Der Gaa.\nGs banoslt ii6 DsrmutIi4 I'm Elm.\nae1nli4teit.\n\n\n.Nber.\n\n\nGttpas ipie cine left, llnseoulb Ipies\ng.Ite fi9 in 6sn 3iisen oes Germ.\nnSt. per