{"parentUuid":"31abea3a-919b-4b65-b7ab-0a552c2bbadd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"775e54ef-6487-4f79-8598-643421b87718","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, Bash, Edit, Monitor, Read, SendMessage, Skill, TaskStop, ToolSearch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__browser_batch, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__find, mcp__Claude_Browser__get_page_text, mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__tabs_close, mcp__ccd_pr__get_status, mcp__ccd_session__mark_chapter, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n**Setup.**\n- This is a child session of the EM session `local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e`, on Paper Ghosts: repo `Hotragn/Paperghosts` at `/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts`, branch `phase-2c-reader`.\n- Hand-over notes go to `/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-X.md`; `step-2C.1.md` has been written.\n- Every turn ends with `mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up`, then a closing message. Use `mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan` for the task list.\n\n**Standing and security rules (verbatim where possible):**\n- \"never print, log or echo secrets from `.env`, and check keys by shape only\"\n- \"No global installs and no Homebrew\"\n- \"Stop and ask before anything public (repo visibility, deploys, DNS, posting) or any spending beyond free tiers and existing credits\"\n- \"Make small commits on phase branches and open pull requests into `main`; I merge them\"\n- \"Record numbered decisions in `Docs/DECISIONS.md`, and end each milestone with a STATUS block in `Docs/RESUME.md`\"\n- \"Entire capture is enabled through `.claude/settings.json`; don't touch it\"\n- \"Don't run brainstorming Q&A with the owner; put questions in your reply to me\"\n- \"Start every reply to me with `<step>: DONE` or `<step>: BLOCKED — reason`, then 150 words at most\". For this step the first line is `2C.2: GATE PASSED` or `2C.2: BLOCKED — <reason>`.\n- Scope pgrep/ps to my uid; never print the hostname; filter push output with `grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\"`.\n- Before every commit:\n  - `git diff --cached > $S/staged-X.diff`\n  - `uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged-X.diff` (names only)\n  - `grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" <diff>`\n- Library of Congress requests:\n  - one at a time, never in parallel\n  - each cached\n  - www.loc.gov at least 3.5 s apart; tile.loc.gov at 1 s\n  - a CAPTCHA (HTML) answer counts as busy and is never cached\n- \"Never touch sample_mflix or any other database\"\n- \"check claims like 'pushed' with `ls-remote` before you report them\"\n- Commits end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`. PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n- No PR until 2C closes. \"Commit and push at each natural point, so a limit costs nothing.\"\n- \"No model output of any kind may touch gold or dev until the labels are frozen: not the teacher, not base 4B, not Backboard.\"\n- Scratch: `S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad`.\n\n**Current task: 2C.2, the labels** (persona: ML specialist, as labeller).\n1. Commit POLICY v2 first (done).\n2. Label all 300 gold (done) and all 150 dev myself (in progress).\n   - Read the crop wherever the OCR is unclear.\n   - Every label passes the page's `checked()`, quotes and choices included.\n   - Record each article's E-slices.\n3. **Blind second pass:** reading agents label every gold article again, and a seeded 20% of dev.\n   - They see only the text, its crop on request, and POLICY: no first labels, strata or weights.\n   - Report agreement before adjudication, each with an interval:\n     - raw agreement and Cohen's kappa on kind\n     - agreement on report or not\n     - agreement per field on articles both call reports\n   - Adjudicate every disagreement under POLICY, keeping both labels and the ruling.\n4. **Freeze:** commit `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` with their sha256s, before any model output exists.\n5. **Measure on gold:**\n   - reports per stratum and in all, against the 35.3 expected\n   - the weighted report rate\n   - the story-place rule, scored against the labelled `place_state`\n- Commit labels in batches as I go.\n- **Gate:**\n  - 450 labels, all passing `checked()`\n  - the second pass's agreement, with intervals\n  - every disagreement adjudicated\n  - label hashes committed before any model output\n  - the story-place rule measured\n  - decision 38 written\n  - tests and lint pass\n  - pushed and checked with `ls-remote`\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **Tooling:**\n  - uv with Python 3.12; ruff (`make lint` also runs the pnpm web lint and tsc); pytest (`make test`; 365 passed at the last full run)\n  - FastAPI with TestClient; zstd JSONL data\n  - `paperghosts.stats.wilson(hits, n)` returns (low, high)\n- **The split** (decision 37): `eval/gold/split.json` with sha256 `2593375…836c7`, in `eval/gold/HASH` as `<sha>  split.json`.\n  - 300 gold and 150 dev in 17 strata.\n  - Each item has `article_id`, `stratum`, `date`, `group`, `pi` and `weight`.\n  - The split also holds the quarantine (1,201 flags on 1,196 articles) and `out_of_pool` (6,567 articles).\n- **Inclusive grouping:** `reprints.groups`. Leakage rule: LEAK=0.10 and FEWEST=5 whole-text five-word runs.\n- **POLICY.md v2** (6ef55ca):\n  - rule 19, spirit-adjacent claims\n  - signals where rules 6 and 9 meet\n  - rule 16: where several items are reports, fields come from the item with the lexicon's match, else the first\n  - place_type in the schema's values: `inn_or_hotel`, `road_or_bridge`, `public_building`\n  - the label record's `slices`: E1–E14 except E9, which comes from the grouping\n  - a dated Changes section\n  - 19 rules in all\n- **Label record keys:** `article_id`, `kind`, `kind_quote`, `place`, `place_state`, `seen`, `outcome`, `specific_place`, `place_type`, `precision` (each `{value, quote}` or null), `people` (a list), `rules`, `slices`, `crop_used`, `note`, `labeller`, `labelled_at`.\n- **Labelling conventions applied to gold (use the same for dev):**\n  - **Report:** told as happened, tied to a particular person, place or occasion. This includes:\n    - claims inside essays (rule 6) and printed-as-fact narratives\n    - a prankster taken for a ghost (outcome `hoax`)\n    - apparitions of the living when a figure is seen\n    - séances or ouija sittings told with messages (rule 4), and jokey genuine reports (rule 8)\n  - **Fiction:** tales with a narrator's framing, serials, poems, jokes and quips.\n  - **Idiom:** figurative uses, including haunts as places frequented, political ghosts and the ghost of a chance.\n  - **Religious:** the Holy Ghost, sermons, church notices, the Ghost Dance, Caodaism.\n  - **Advert:** mediums' cards and classifieds, patent medicine, book lists, theatre and record puffs, Mumler's photos.\n  - **Other:**\n    - names (horses, teams, nicknames, a man surnamed Haunting)\n    - OCR accidents (flaunt read as haunt, mounted read as haunted, hunt read as haunt, Spaak read as Spook)\n    - literal knocks; obituaries with \"spirit land\"\n    - spiritualism news with no phenomenon (rule 15); séances announced for later (rule 4); French séance as a sitting\n    - general essays (rule 6); superstitions in general and telepathic dreams with no figure (rule 19)\n  - **Outcomes:**\n    - `unknown` quotes the closing sentence\n    - `explained` for a natural cause or delusion\n    - `unexplained` for no cause found or \"remains to be seen\"\n    - `hoax` for a deliberate deception\n  - **place_state** only from the text or the dateline, never inferred.\n  - **Slices:**\n    - E1: Holy Ghost\n    - E2: ghost idioms and haunt-as-frequented\n    - E3: ghost fiction, serials and Christmas stories, including ghost poems\n    - E4: theatre adverts, patent medicine, puffs\n    - E5: séances, rappings, medium notices and ads, ouija\n    - E6: hoaxes, pranks and exposures\n    - E7: humour\n    - E8: phantom ships, trains and lights\n    - E10: garbled OCR\n    - E11: merged items\n    - E12: non-English\n    - E13: surname or place name\n    - E14: political figures of speech\n- **Quote pitfalls:** OCR line breaks split words (\"Per sons\"); OCR letter swaps (\"u supposed ghost\"); quotes are checked against `squeezed(headline + \"\\n\" + text)`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n**`paperghosts/cluster/reprints.py`**\n- `shingles(text, window=WINDOW, sample=SAMPLE)` takes window and sample options (1c8d670).\n- `groups(doc_keys, doc_body, boilerplate=BOILERPLATE)` (ba85e04):\n  ```python\n  return clusters([pairs(set(k)) | pairs(set(b)) for k, b in zip(doc_keys, doc_body, strict=True)], boilerplate)\n  ```\n\n**`scripts/check_leakage.py`** (ba85e04, 984ae90)\n- Constants: `LEAK, FEWEST = 0.10, 5`; `ARCHIVE = Path(\"data\",\"archive\",\"lexicon-v1\",\"samples\")`.\n- Functions:\n  - `runs`, `flagged`, `near_misses`, `frame(root)` (ids, dates, group, candidates count), `examples(root)` (POLICY ids by regex)\n  - `paths_of`, `texts_in`, `whole_texts(root, wanted, paths=None)`\n  - `hold` and `leaks_in`, which use `np.searchsorted` against the sorted held runs\n  - `leaks(root, held, excluded, workers=8)`, `between(a, b)`, `crossings(found, gold, dev, held, out)`\n  - `check(root)`, which also covers `examples_unread` and `examples_reprinted`\n  - `justify(root)` and `main`\n- Results: `eval/results/phase2c/leakage.json` (passed) and `leakage_threshold.json` (603 of 603).\n\n**`scripts/gold_draw.py`** (984ae90)\n- RULES rarest first; SHIPS, HOAX, FOREIGN and ENGLISH regexes; the ALLOCATION of 17 strata.\n- Functions: `stratum(row)`, `systematic(units, n, rng)`, `take`, `items`, `members`, `decades`, `rate_class`, `judged_rates`, `expected`, `main`.\n- Results: `eval/results/phase2c/gold_draw.json`, with expected reports 35.3 (14.0–86.5).\n\n**`scripts/label_gold.py`** (06fe6cb, 7c13f64, 2d583b5)\n- Modes:\n  - `serve [labeller]` on 127.0.0.1:8765\n  - `crops`: warms `data/gold/crops.json`, one article at a time\n  - `show SPLIT N [labeller]`\n  - `check FILE`\n  - `save FILE [labeller]`\n- Constants: `SLICES` is parsed from POLICY with `^  - (E\\d+): (.+)$`; `OUT = {\"gold\": GOLD/\"labels.jsonl\", \"dev\": GOLD/\"dev_labels.jsonl\"}`; `SEEN = ROOT/\"data\"/\"gold\"/\"crops.json\"`.\n- Functions: `order_of(rows)` (seeded shuffle `\"2C.1 labelling order {name}\"`), `warm`, `show`, `save_file`, `checked(label, row, labeller)`, `save` (one label per article and labeller), `app(rows, labeller, crops_for, out, crop_dir)`.\n- `save` routes by `rows[aid][\"split\"]`, so dev labels go to `dev_labels.jsonl` automatically.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/test_reprints.py`, `tests/test_check_leakage.py`, `tests/test_gold_draw.py`, and `tests/test_label_gold.py` (5 tests: page, save, refusals and slices, save_file, show blindness).\n\n**`eval/gold/POLICY.md`**: version 2 (6ef55ca). The new rule 19 examples:\n- 2_1853 (Greek burial custom)\n- 7_1913 (whale omen)\n- 17_1900 (dowsing as clairvoyance)\n- 5_1902 (crystal gazing)\n\n**`eval/gold/labels.jsonl`**: 300 labels by labeller \"Claude\", committed in batches; the last is 05d7325.\n\n**Docs**\n- `Docs/DECISIONS.md`: decision 37 (fc26372), plus the quarantine-count note (402de83).\n- `Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md`: 2C notes (the pooled recall screen; the 2C.4 recheck at 0.05 and 4 runs) and 2D notes (short texts' weak links; \"measure these changes\").\n- `Docs/RESUME.md`: the next step updated.\n\n**Label scripts** in `$S/labels/`:\n- `common.py`: `q(value, quote)`, `label(aid, kind, kq, rules=(), slices=(), note=\"\", crop=False, **fields)`, `write(labels, path)`.\n- Batch files g01.py–g15.py and fix01.py, each written to `.jsonl`.\n- Workflow: run the `.py` to write the `.jsonl`; `uv run python scripts/label_gold.py check $S/labels/X.jsonl`; then `save … Claude`; then commit with the scan.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n- **The leak scan was too slow.** `np.intersect1d` re-sorted the held runs for each article. I stopped the task and switched to a `searchsorted` binary search; 1900 now scans in 4.3 s and the full draw takes 196 s.\n- **Fixture error in the crossings test:** the test's fixture was wrong, not the code; fixed.\n- **Lint:**\n  - B905: zip calls given `strict=True`.\n  - FURB167: `re.I` replaced with `re.IGNORECASE`.\n  - Formatting fixed.\n- **Mutation-check slips:**\n  - A sed didn't match the multi-line RULES tuple, so the plant was redone in Python.\n  - One mutation left the file mutated because an assert failed mid-loop; restored from the keep copy.\n- **Quote failures, fixed against the text as printed:**\n  - \"Per sons who passed there at midnight\"\n  - \"u supposed ghost which haunts n lumber camp\"\n- **The census script** hit BrokenProcessPool without a `__main__` guard; fixed.\n- **Running `sleep` in Bash was blocked;** used Monitor with an until-loop instead.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n- **2C.1's gate passed.** The EM accepted it.\n- **Quarantine counts reconciled:** 1,201 flags on 1,196 distinct articles, because 5 pool articles each reprint two held ones.\n- **POLICY's three missing examples** were found in lexicon v1's archived random samples. All 63 examples are compared with gold and dev; none is reprinted there.\n- **Gold labelling is complete:** 45 reports, against 35.3 expected.\n- **The grouping missed some reprints within gold:** the backwoods preacher sketch has two printings in gold (batches 9 and 10). That's allowed within gold and worth noting.\n- **The crop warm-up** runs in the background; the last count was 296 articles warmed. A page check failed for 14_1913 and 11_1894 (\"words aren't in its boxes\"), and 42_1923 has too few words to check.\n\n6. All user messages:\n- **The EM's message accepting 2C.1** (summarized in full in item 1):\n  - checks passed at fc26372; reconcile 1,196 vs 1,201\n  - items 1 to 5: keep the draw with no redraw, and add a pooled recall screen to the plan's step 7; dev labelled by me, yes; item 3 fine; fix place_type's spelling; put short texts' weak links in the 2D notes\n  - the POLICY amendments as one dated commit before any label\n  - notes for 2C.4 and step 7\n  - the 2C.2 brief and gate, quoted above\n- **Earlier EM messages** (before the prior summary): the 2C.1 brief and the resume instruction.\n- **Repeated system notes:** \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\"\n- **\"Tool loaded.\"** acknowledgements.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Label the 150 dev articles in batches of 20, committing `eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl` each time. Dev batch 1 is written to `$S/c1/d01.txt`.\n- **The blind second pass.** Its requirements:\n  - every gold article plus a seeded 20% of dev, 30 articles\n  - reading agents in parallel, each writing its own JSONL in scratch, blind (no labels.jsonl, split.json or gold_draw.json)\n  - crops from the cache only (pre-warmed), so no parallel LoC requests\n  - each agent validates with `label_gold.py check`; then save sequentially with labeller \"second pass\"\n- **Agreement:** raw agreement and Cohen's kappa on kind with intervals; report-or-not agreement; per-field agreement on articles both call reports (quote-overlap or value match). Adjudicate every disagreement, saving a \"ruling\" labeller record with the reason, and keep both labels.\n- **Freeze:** HASH gains the sha256 lines for `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl`; commit before any model output.\n- **Measure on gold:**\n  - reports per stratum and in all, against 35.3\n  - the weighted report rate (Σw·report / Σw)\n  - the story-place rule, implemented as code finding the state from the text or dateline, scored against the labelled place_state, and compared with the paper's-state fallback\n- Compute E9 from the grouping and count slices.\n- Write decision 38 (including the apparitions-of-the-living call, and the within-gold reprint the grouping missed); update RESUME.\n- Run `make test` and `make lint`; push; check with `ls-remote`. Write the hand-over note `step-2C.2.md` and report with `2C.2: GATE PASSED`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n- All 300 gold articles are labelled and committed (05d7325): \"Gold labels, first pass: the last batch, all 300 gold articles\".\n- The plan advanced to step 5, \"Label all 150 dev articles\".\n- I then ran:\n  ```\n  uv run python scripts/label_gold.py show dev 20 | sed -e 's/^crops: \\[.*\\]$/crops: cached/' > $S/c1/d01.txt\n  ```\n  It produced 1,668 lines and 8,019 words. It hasn't been read or labelled yet.\n- The plan steps:\n  1. Reconcile the quarantine count and add the plan notes (done)\n  2. Commit POLICY v2 and the page's slices (done)\n  3. Build the labelling batch and save tools (done)\n  4. Label all 300 gold articles in batches (done)\n  5. Label all 150 dev articles (in progress)\n  6. Run the blind second pass with reading agents\n  7. Measure agreement, adjudicate, and freeze\n  8. Measure reports and the story-place rule\n  9. Write decision 38, test, lint and push\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nRead `$S/c1/d01.txt` and label dev batch 1, following the EM's instruction: \"Label all 300 gold and 150 dev yourself. Read the crop wherever the OCR is unclear. Every label passes the page's `checked()`, quotes and choices included. Record each article's E-slices… Commit labels in batches as you go.\"\n- Write `$S/labels/d01.py` with `common.py`'s helpers.\n- Run `label_gold.py check`, then `save … Claude`; dev articles route to `eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl`.\n- Commit with the diff scan, push, and continue with `show dev 20` for batches 2 to 8.\n- Keep the gold conventions above, so the gold and dev labels agree.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/hotragn/.claude/projects/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"be4286a1-7474-4ffd-8817-f4a0c09fb5af","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:10:10.281Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":45},"turnOrigin":"peer","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
