bers Of this organization already\n606\thave been made, including Editor CAL\n607\tlay two lawyers ar-l non-commis-\n608\tstoned officer OF the imperial navy\n609\tknown as Kovacz. alias karacsony\n610\t\n611\t\n612\tThe latter already has admitted that\n613\the received hand grenades from Gallay,\n614\tbut asserts that he had nothing to do\n615\twith the Liberal Club outrage and re-\n616\tfuses steadfastly TO betray who did the\n617\tbombing.\n618\t\n619\t\n620\tStrange rumors are afloat that the\n621\tpolice first received intimation Of the\n622\tcompletely OF the \"Awaking Magyars\n623\tthrough a spiritualistic seance. in which\n624\tthe medium described the men who laid\n625\tthe bombs and gave the details OF their\n626\tmovements following the attempt which\n627\twere then easily traced by the police.\n628\t\n629\t\n630\tSo far ten members OF the \"Awakin2\n631\tMagyars\" have been confiped in cells,\n632\tbut II Is doubted whether the Govern\n633\tment will be able successfully to COM\n634\tbat this new commorra. which already\n635\tis supported by a strong section OF the\n636\tBudapest public.\n637\t\n638\t=== 31_1921-10-31_p1_sn86072160_00514150382_1921103101_0538.json\n639\tNone · 1921-10-31\n640\tcrops: faro_1921/1921-10-31_p1_sn86072160_00514150382_1921103101_0538.json: too few words to check\n641\theadline: sPoOK PARTY.\n642\t---\n643\tSP0OK PARTY.\n644\tWhere? Methodist church.\n645\tWhen7 October 81.\n646\tBy whom7 Epworth league.\n647\tComet You are welcome. 1o.3I.lt.\n648\t\n649\t=== 8_1900-08-10_pna_sn90059182_00393341087_1900081001_0258.json\n650\tThe Ely miner. [volume] (Ely, Minn.) 1895-1986 · 1900-08-10\n651\tcrops: cached\n652\theadline: GHOSTS PLAINLY VISIBLE.\n653\t\n654\tSome People Said to Be Consti.\n655\ttuted That They See Super\n656\t\n657\t\n658\tnatural Beings,\n659\t---\n660\tThere is no doubt that person may\n661\tapparently see objects and hear words\n662\twhich another person close by cannot\n663\tsee or hear. Such impressions are to\n664\tbe referred not to actually existing OBJ.\n665\tjects, but to the action of the subjects\n666\tmind, says the Westminster Review.\n667\tDR.. Abercromby tells of one patient\n668\twho could, by directing his attention\n669\tto an idea, call up to sight the appro.\n670\tpirate image or scene, though the thing\n671\tcalled up were an object he had never\n672\tseen. but had merely imagined. When\n673\tmeeting friend in the street he could\n674\tnot be sure whether the appearance\n675\twas his friend or a specter illusion till\n676\the had tried to touch it and had heard\n677\tthe voice. Goethe saw an exact coun.\n678\tterpart of himself advancing toward\n679\thim, an experience repeated by Wilkie\n680\tCollins. Sir Walter Scott relates that\n681\tsoon after the death of Lord Byron he\n682\tread an account of the deceased poet.\n683\tOn stepping into the hall immedia tely\n684\tafter he saw right before him il\n685\tstanding posture the exact representa-.\n686\tton of his departed friend, whose rec.\n687\tobjection had been so strongly brought\n688\tto his Imagination. After stopping\n689\tmoment to note the extraordinary re-\n690\tsemblance he advanced toward it and\n691\tthe figure gradually disappeared.\n692\t\n693\t\n694\tSome of the cases narrated by Sir\n695\tDavid Brewster are particularly in.\n696\tstructive. The subject was lady (Mrs.\n697\tAl and her hallucina tons were care.\n698\tfully studied by her husband and Sir\n699\tDavid. On one occasion she saw her\n700\thusband, as she thought, who had\n701\tgone out half an hour before, standing\n702\twithin two feet of her in the drawing.\n703\troom. She was astonished to receive\n704\tno response when she spoke to him.\n705\tShe remembered that Sir David had told\n706\ther to press one eyeball with the finger.\n707\twhen the impression of any real objeo,\n708\twould be doubled. She tried to appl .\n709\tthe test, but the figure walked awa5\n710\tand disappeared. The simple scientific,\n711\texperiment diverted her attention frorl\n712\tthe creation of her mind, and this, NJ\n713\tlonger being in sole possession, could\n714\tnot maintain Itself and was dissolved.\n715\tAnother hallucination took the form\n716\tof her dead sister-in-law. The figure\n717\tappeared in a dress which Mrs. A. had\n718\tnever seen, but which had been de.\n719\tscribed to her by common friend.\n720\t\n721\t=== 12_1900-11-08_pna_sn78000873_00279524834_1900110801_0363.json\n722\tThe Republican journal. [volume] (Belfast, Me.) 1829-current · 1900-11-08\n723\tcrops: None\n724\theadline: THE NEWS OF BELFAST.\n725\t---\n726\t.ba Howes block for use as photograph\n727\tp-nre room\n728\t\n729\t\n730\taIa lose Co. has fitted its hose car\n731\tS'' .+b q pole for two horses, in place of\n732\t''5 bsfts formerly used.\n733\t\n734\t\n735\tcommissioner Robbins is gravel\n736\t\n737\t\n738\thang section of High street, getting\n739\tA- ..l from &. G. Abbott's bank near\n740\t.s- Stand\n741\t\n742\t\n743\tA.-r Whitney has built a new hen\n744\t\n745\t\n746\t,th some convenient features. The\n747\tp'' 49,. III fed and the eggs gathered with\n748\t...a. INTO the pen.\n749\t\n750\t\n751\t,.I..n for the cottage Mr.. II. L. KOcher-\n752\t.l IF hicago proposes to build on\n753\t\n754\t\n755\tfont, Northport. calls for build\n756\t\n757\t\n758\tra4t ang, with the first story of stone.\n759\t~ r.pdon Manufacturing Co. has a new\n760\t.so oa the road in charge of R. c. Allen,\n761\t1s harness dressing, soap and axle oil.\n762\t\n763\t\n764\t,ll but on an additional two-hOrse\n765\t.smu,E- prins'\n766\t\n767\t\n768\t.54r, report a brisk demand and\n769\t\n770\t\n771\tfir-, for mink, but say that other\n772\t.tfn are not yet in condition, and\n773\t\n774\t\n775\ttnpters and others to wait awhile\n776\tal. il-to improve.\n777\t\n778\t\n779\t1t a-d of Registration found that II\n780\t\n781\t\n782\t. .... to ne stricken from the voting\n783\t\n784\t\n785\taided, for the November cleo\n786\t\n787\t\n788\t,..- a>, of l. 