pression of faith In his\npower to avert whatever evil might be\nlurking around under cover OF the\ndarkness, elected a tender reassuring\npat from his disengaged left member\nand her half-stified gasp of nervous\nness ended in a sigh of satisfaction\nborn of the knowledge that he was\nthere and able to protect her. She had\ncome to the meeting expecting to have\nmomentous questions settled which\nhad been troubling her for several\nweeks and the prospect of immediate\ncommunication with unseen messen-\ngers from the spirit land overawed\nher with an unwonted sense OF SOL\nemnity.\n\n\np, They sat there for a minute or more\nenveloped in Cimmerian darkness and\ntomblike silence. At last a. man in an\nother corner of the room raised ms\ncracked voice to the tune of He VIII\nSave You,\" and invited the inhabi-\ntants of the world beyond to show\nyour faces just now\"\n\n\nwhen you feel the trumpet touch\nyou speak to the visiting spirit\" said\nthe medium, otherwise ii will not\n| stay\"\n\n\nThey waited again for some mani\n| festation. At the expiration of the\n| second period of expectancy meek\nsister struck up a hymn expressive at\n| once of deep devotion, alteration ana\n| contrition, and the woman Joined In\n| with her conscience divided against\n| itself as to whether such method or\n4 worship. were sacrllege or a sanctified\n4 expression of the most profound faltn.\n/ The last stanza died away In a trem-\n| bling and long-doawn out note. AT\n| that moment three distinct taps on\nher knees aroused the woman 10 the\n| fact that the critical time had come\n| and she grasped her companions hand\nstill more tightly.\n\n\nWhat is it? What do you want?''\n| she asked, family.\n\n\n| There was a series OF inG4stinc'\n| gasps and murmurs, which gave COM\n| nonsense listeners the impression\nthat the ghostly visitor had lef'\n| mart of his breath behind him in his\n| scra mble to reach shores terrestrial. A,\nlast there floated up from the depths\n| of the trumpet the one word, Harry.\n| She emitted a frightened little scream\n| and drew vet nearer to the man beside\nher.\n\n\nmy husband\" she walled in &\nvoice made weak by terror.\n\n\nTalk to him.\" whispered the man\ngravely.\n\n\nShe fought for composure and SPOKE\nagain. 49,,\n\n\n\"Harry.\" she pleaded meekly, \"tel\n\n\noeEteu me truly. Did you mean wha\nvou said Just before you died abou\nNV marrying again? Do you thinl\nthat was just right? l am very lionel!\nsome times, you know\"\n\n\nAfter the usual prelude OF labore'\nrespiration the far-away voice sounde'\nclearly and distinctly throughout tn\n| room. ., -,\n\n\nII want you to marry at once\" ]\n| said II shall never be happy unit\nyou have done so.\n\n\nThe lights flashed up with suddel\n| brilliancy and the woman leaned owe\nAGAINST the mans shoulder and yer,\n| appropriately tainted. The whole ba\nker's dozen of them pronounced II IN\n\n\nmost remarkable meeting they ma\never attended. When the party orok\n\n\nnm and the little band of seekers afte\n\n\nspiritual truth paid the usual zee IN\n\n\nman who doubted slipped an extra u\nbill into the mediums HANDS.\n\n\nyou've made everything plain SAL\ning for me from this time on, ne sai\n! payly. \"and / consider your service\ncheap at this price\n","numLines":1937,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1937}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5dcf3fe3-82a5-4909-99da-ed97b46d7d23","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
