om.\", [12, 13], [], \"a steamer's timetable; the Phantom is its name\"),\nlabel(\"9_1930-01-27_p10_sn84026749_0022225467A_1930012701_0563.json\", \"other\", \"The stage show, Haunting a\", [13], [], \"a theatre review; flaunting read as Haunting\"),\nlabel(\"4_1904-06-16_pna_sn86082061_00415629710_1904061601_0913.json\", \"fiction\", \"said the lively boarder\", [9, 10], [], \"a lively boarder's sketch of a mirror-drawing trick; a planchette's markings as a simile\"),\nlabel(\"1_1842-01-01_p1_sn86058217_00271744742_1842010101_0405.json\", \"other\", \"steam ship IT medium size\", [], [], \"the Navy Secretary's report; medium and spirit in their ordinary senses\"),\nlabel(\"12_1942-11-26_p40_sn83045462_00280603296_1942112601_0163.json\", \"idiom\", \"Wraith-like gallops after kicks\", [10], [\"E2\"], \"a football back's punt returns\"),\nlabel(\"3_1922-04-23_p27_sn83045774_00271744262_1922042301_0817.json\", \"report\", \"through a spiritualistic seance\", [4], [\"E5\"], \"a rumoured seance whose medium described the Budapest bombers; no place given for the sitting\",\n    people=[q(\"the medium\", \"the medium described the men\"), q(\"the police\", \"the police first received intimation\")],\n    seen=q(\"the medium's description of the men who laid the bombs and their movements\", \"the medium described the men who laid the bombs\"),\n    outcome=q(\"unknown\", \"supported by a strong section OF the Budapest public\")),\nlabel(\"31_1921-10-31_p1_sn86072160_00514150382_1921103101_0538.json\", \"other\", \"By whom7 Epworth league.\", [13], [], \"an Epworth League Halloween party notice\"),\nlabel(\"8_1900-08-10_pna_sn90059182_00393341087_1900081001_0258.json\", \"report\", \"Sir Walter Scott relates that soon after the death of Lord Byron\", [2, 6], [], \"an essay on hallucinations from the Westminster Review, with particular cases; fields from the first ghost of the dead, Scott's sight of Byron\",\n    place=q(\"the hall\", \"stepping into the hall\"),\n    people=[q(\"Sir Walter Scott\", \"Sir Walter Scott\")],\n    seen=q(\"the exact likeness of his dead friend Lord Byron, standing\", \"the exact representa-. ton of his departed friend\"),\n    outcome=q(\"explained\", \"so strongly brought to his Imagination\")),\nlabel(\"12_1900-11-08_pna_sn78000873_00279524834_1900110801_0363.json\", \"other\", \"with dim lights, ghost\", [13, 15, 17], [\"E10\"], \"Belfast local items, badly garbled, no crop: Halloween parties with ghosts, and a Spiritualists' meeting with addresses; no claim can be read\"),\nlabel(\"9_1910-08-07_pna_sn85038615_00100480153_1910080701_0221.json\", \"religious\", \"Ghost. Amen.\", [11], [\"E1\"], \"an essay on faith; a medieval certificate in the name of the Holy Ghost\"),\nlabel(\"31_1870-08-24_pna_sn85033221_00514152378_1870082401_0504.json\", \"idiom\", \"saw ghosts and hob-goblins\", [10], [\"E14\"], \"editorial paragraphs; a rival paper's fears over the land grant\"),\nlabel(\"9_1900-11-30_p1_sn98060035_00202199203_1900113001_0222.json\", \"advert\", \"Spirit, Medium and Occult\", [12], [\"E5\"], \"a clairvoyant palmist's advertisement\"),\nlabel(\"21_1839-10-03_pna_sn84026897_00237288336_1839100301_0136.json\", \"fiction\", \"The Sons of Genius\", [9], [], \"a letter giving Humphry Davy's poem; the pallid spectres of the night\"),\nlabel(\"13_1905-08-27_pna_sn85042104_00332892393_1905082701_0522.json\", \"other\", \"Seance d'adieu\", [4], [], \"the Portsmouth peace conference; a French seance as a sitting\"),\nlabel(\"10_1886-11-10_pna_sn85025431_00212479792_1886111001_0411.json\", \"report\", \"the ghostly team dashed by\", [6, 14], [\"E8\"], \"printed as fact from the Baltimore American, with initialled witnesses; a rector and a friend see the dead judge's carriage pass three times and vanish in his lane; a phantom vehicle\",\n    place=q(\"near Judge S.'s gate, on the Eastern Shore\", \"not far from Judge SIS gate\"),\n    people=[q(\"the Rev. Dr. B.\", \"the Rev. DR.. B.\"), q(\"a friend\", \"in