526\twa'chman: II believe in spirits and\n1527\tghosts. l known such exist. II YOU will\n1528\tGame up III April I will convince you\"\n1529\tde then told Of the phantorn train that\n1530\tevery year comes up the road with the\n1531\tbody ol Abraham Lincoln Regularly\n1532\t10 the month Of Apr,l. about midnight,\n1533\ttue aIr ON the tack becomes very keen\n1534\tand eating. On either side Il It iS warm\n1535\tand still, Every watchmau when he feels\n1536\tthis air steps of the track and sits down\n1537\tTO watch. Soon alter the pilot engine,\n1538\twith long black streamers, and o band\n1539\twith Instruments, playing drges, grip-\n1540\tning skeletons sitting allbout, will pass\n1541\tup nolSelessly, and the very air grows\n1542\tblack. lit Is moonlight clouds always\n1543\tcome over the moon, and the music seems\n1544\tTO liDger, as Il frozen with horror. A\n1545\tfew moments after and the phantom\n1546\ttrain glides by. Flags and streamerS\n1547\thang about The track ahead seems GOV.\n1548\tcred with u black carpet, and the wheels\n1549\tare drsped with the same. The coflnS Of\n1550\tthe murdered Lincoln Is seen lying on\n1551\tthe centre ola car, and oil about It in the\n1552\tair and the train behind are vast numbers\n1553\tOf bluecoated men, some with coffin on\n1554\ttheir backs, others leaning on them. It\n1555\tseems then that I'LL the vast armies that\n1556\tdied during the war are escorting the\n1557\tphantom train ot the President. The wind\n1558\ti blowing, dies away at once, and over all\n1559\tthe earth solemn hush, almost sitting,\n1560\tprevails. ia train were passing, It's noise\n1561\twould be drowned in the silence, and the\n1562\tphantom train would ride over ii. Clocks\n1563\tand watches always stop. and when look\n1564\tcd \" are found to be from Ave to elghts\n1565\tminutes behind. Everywhere on;the rad\n1566\tabout the 27th, Of April, the ttmeiof\n1567\twatches and trains Is found suddenly bO.\n1568\thind. This, said the leading watchmau,\n