n evidence produced Mr.. Maskelyne,\n696\tan expert, who fully explained the \"slate\n697\ttrick )\" and Mr.. 81 ade has been sentenced to\n698\tthree months imprisonment.\n699\t\n700\t\n701\tAt lecture delivered in Boston Music\n702\tHall, on Saturday evening, Ash inst Mr..\n703\tIrving Bishop, Of New York, went through\n704\tthe whole range Of spifitualistic tricks,\n705\tfully explaining that they were ali neither\n706\tmore nor less than feats of jugglery. Some\n707\tof the tests to WHICH be submitted, such as\n708\tthe playing on instumenrs with his hands\n709\tand feet tied in the cabinet, were very se-\n710\twe're, but we're all successfully performed.\n711\tSince then Mr.. Bishop has made the round\n712\tof the Boston mediums whom he exposes\n713\twith his usual ability. He is doing useful\n714\twork, for which he deserves the thanks of\n715\tthe public.\n716\t\n717\t=== 2_1895-10-26_p1_sn99068076_00415623379_1895102601_0707.json\n718\tThe Kimball graphic. (Kimball, Brule County, Dakota [S.D.]) 1883-1905 · 1895-10-26\n719\tcrops: None\n720\theadline: Political\n721\t---\n722\tThe young enthusiast in politics went\n723\tto offer his services for the campaign to\n724\tan old wheel-horse who had seen serv-\n725\tice aud done it, too, before the youth\n726\twas born.\n727\t\n728\t\n729\t\"What can you do?\" asked the vet\n730\teran.\n731\t\n732\t\n733\tIl can raise my voice in defense Of\n734\tprinciples AL over the state\" was\n735\tthe proud reply.\n736\t\n737\t\n738\t\"Um- UNI err yes err anything\n739\telse?\"\n740\t\n741\t\n742\tIl can raise party clubs everywhere\"\n743\tMISUNDERSTANDING elseP\"\n744\t\n745\t\n746\tIl can raise the spirit of patriotism in\n747\tevery village\"\n748\t\n749\t\n750\t\"Um-yes-anvthing elseP\"\n751\t\n752\t\n753\tu can raise the standard of revolt\n754\tagainst corruption\"\n755\t\n756\t\n757\t\"Ah! Um-ycs-anything elseP\"\n758\t\n759\t\n760\tThe young mans enthusiasm was\n761\tJared.\n762\t\n763\t\n764\tGreat Caesar\" he exclaimed, ISN'T\n765\tthat enough?\"\n766\t\n767\t\n768\tHardly\"\n769\t\n770\t\n771\t.What more could you want?-\n772\t\n773\t\n774\tCan you raise $40. 00O?\" asked the\n775\tveteran, in a profoundly yearning tone.\n776\tand the enthusiast vanished with his\n777\tenthusi y rot Free Press.\n778\t\n779\t=== 50_1914-03-02_pna_sn83045462_00280658881_1914030201_0282.json\n780\tEvening star. [volume] (Washington, D.C.) 1854-1972 · 1914-03-02\n781\tcrops: None\n782\theadline: SPIRITUALISM.\n783\t---\n784\tMEETINGS MONDAY, WEDNESDAY. FRIDAY\n785\t\n786\t\n787\tpm. sharp; q message each: daily read\n788\tiRgs. Mrs. J. T.. MAI.TBl. So1 Mi Vernon pi.\n789\tNV. back Of Carnegie Library. Phone NJ sos.\n790\t\n791\t=== 7_1922-03-11_p1_sn85038022_00202195027_1922031101_0244.json\n792\tThe public ledger. [volume] (Maysville, Ky.) 1913-1968 · 1922-03-11\n793\tcrops: None\n794\theadline: \n795\t---\n796\tOf forty miracle plays all celebrating\n797\tin some way the interventi on of the\n798\tBlessed Virgin, produced back in the\n799\tdays when the theater had its begin\n800\tnings in the church.\n801\t\n802\t\n803\tNy\n804\t\n805\t\n806\tHere are two disappointed immi-\n807\tgrants to our shores who hold no\n808\tgrievance against us because Of\n809\tthreatened deportation. Mr.. and Mrs.\n810\tFilippo Quattrocchi landed en- Ellis\n811\tIsland from Italy recently. Because\n812\tthe husbands health is not good, de-\n813\tportattion was ordered. During an ap-\n814\tpeal from this edict, they have re-\n815\tmanned at the immigration station\n816\tthere on the Island and the other day\n817\twhen a daughter was born to them,\n818\ttthey named her Ellis. That seems\n819\tlike full-hearted appreciation for half\n820\thearted hospitality. rather hope the\n821\tgovernment will decide to stretch a\n822\tpoint and let them stay here.\n823\t\n824\t\n825\tNy\n826\t\n827\t\n828\tPeriwinkle and mimosa are the new\n829\tand popular colors for spring and\n830\tsummer. That was made plain at the\n831\tannu