hat did he mean by thatP\" she\n898\tadded, bending low over her work and\n899\tblushlng deeply.\n900\t\n901\t\n902\t\"He must have meant that the\n903\tyoung baron had done little else than\n904\tfit from one ball and assembly to an\n905\tothor-that he squandered much money\n906\tand INDUCED in countless flirtations.\n907\tOne must not look deeply into the\n908\tlives of men. There are few model\n909\tmon like my cousin\"\n910\t\n911\t\n912\tbut Ussikow looks melancholy and\n913\ti'll. can not understand why he has\n914\tfound no woman to love him and be\n915\tloved by him in return\"\n916\t\n917\t\n918\t\"Hc has found plenty, dear child,\n919\tbut such love lasts on neither side\"\n920\t\n921\t\n922\t\"A love that can not remain true is\n923\tno love at all. This poor man has not\n924\tfound the love he sought\"\n925\t\"Hilmar is not in the least to be\n926\tpiticd, you foolish child. He is happy\n927\tand content. He will some day marry\n928\trich wife. l do not understand why\n929\twomen think him handsome. He can\n930\tin no way compare with my cousin,\n931\twho has the only beauty ncedful in a\n932\tman-that of perfect health.\n933\t\n934\t\n935\t\"But uncle has gray hair and his\n936\twhiskcrs begin\"--\n937\t\n938\t\n939\tTHAT is because he has undergone\n940\tso many fntigues,\" interrupted Mari\n941\tanne, \" because he still studies so\n942\thard He is in all ways the superior\n943\tof Hilmar Won Ussikow. Now let me\n944\ttry on the cap before the glass. 1t is\n945\tcharming. But that ribbon over the\n946\ttop must come off. 1t looks too coquet-\n947\tfish for me-\"\n948\t\n949\t\n950\tThe same hour found Hilmar and\n951\tArnim roaming through the forest, and\n952\ttalking over Hilmar's choice of his fut-\n953\ture home. 1.-The physicians recommend\n954\tthe environs of Lake Geneva\" said the\n955\tinvalid.\n956\t\n957\t\n958\tTHAT is the best air for your nerves.\n959\treplied Arnim. I'm winter you can &C\n960\tover the Alps to Lake Como. With\n961\tprop