y, the\ned Board of Directors was reelected Alba L. Smith,\nfor many years Superintendent of the Hudson River\nRailroad was elected President. The gross receipts\nfor tho year were $GiS7 Sc of which $4,000 u was\nfrom passengers. 1904 81 from freight, and SIS\n6s3 Il from mail service, rents, DC. The total ex-\npenses have been $500 6 81, thus leaving the net\nearnings Sl73,61i 90. The valGe of new property\nadded to the road during the year is estimated at\ne2Q.ss2 &C. The debts Of the Company are estimated\nut Si98G7 CO. and the assets at si08590 16 But the\nsteamboat stock is estimated at only par value, $40\nooo, is claimed worth 90 per cent additional, which\nif conceded would leave a surplus OF assets Of over\nsO000O\n\n\nMr. J. \". Toucey has been appointed General\nSuperintendent Of she Hudson River Road in place\nof A. L. Smith resigned. The appointment will\ngreatly advance the interests Of the road in many\nways.\n\n\nThe New-York Central Road earned IN December\ns075sS7 5s57 Increase $4,000\nAmong the new stock houses is that of II. H. Hollis\nterof No. s Broadst. which unites ample capital\nwith much experience.\n\n\nWithin the years 1906 and 1901 il is said, acct\ndent has happened Oh the line Of the Eric Railway\nBY which the life Of single passenger was lost or\neven endangered\n\n\nThe following are the latest financial advices under\ndate Of December 49, taken from tho circular of\nNessrs. William T. Coleman 65 Co.;\n\n\nThe money market is as wen supplied as ever before\nIT. fact, caUal plentiful loans are made\ncall ut per cent PER month and long loans are\nectcd az ten per cent per annGm on Satisfactory col\nNJ any former period Our farmers have\nparaively wealthy. and spend money for many articles\nseen by reference an article elsewhere columns\nthat the farg products OF California are already nearly\nrapidly and volume surprising all former expeIi\nCnces The Unprecedented yield OF the wheat crop for\nTIC mast two wears nnd the high prices obta