voters.\n663\t\n664\t\n665\tMayor Weaver and the forces now struggling\n666\tto free the city from the grasp of what Secre-\n667\ttary Root recently denounced as corrupt and\n668\tcriminal combination\" wisely directed their en-\n669\tergies toward exposing and undoing the frauds\n670\tIn registration. 1t is needless to say that their\n671\tefforts were hampered at every step by the dis\n672\tcredited but still powerful Republican machine\n673\tMost OF the assessors were put In office by that\n674\tmachine and are still secretly bound to its SER\n675\tvice; but so determined was the pressure Of the\n676\tcity administration through the partly reorgan-\n677\tlied police, and so effective the vigilance of vol\n678\tunteer watchers, that at the September revision\n679\tno less than 1888 electoral ghosts were ree-\n680\tgated once more TO the city cemeteries.\n681\t\n682\t\n683\t1t Is more than likely that many bogus names\n684\tremain for under the lax election laws of Penn\n685\tSylvania the mere payment OF q poll tax may\n686\tcount FOR more In determining a claimants right\n687\tTO vote than proof or lack OF proof Of bona fde\n688\tresidence. 1t may take two or three years to\n689\tweed out lists so easily falsified and so difficult\n690\tOF correction; but the friends of honest govern\n691\tment have accomplished a notable work In ex-\n692\tposing the wholesale frauds perpetrated by the\n693\tmachine and In stripping that machine of\n694\tlarge fraction Of its most useful and loyaI fol-\n695\tlowing. Philadelphia has begun wisely by at\n696\tlacking the weak spot in the organizations\n697\tarmor; but that organization power for evil\n698\tis only to be annulled by overwhelming IL this\n699\tfall at the polls, and then securing personal\n700\tregistration law, which will end all forms of\n701\tvoting by proxy.\n702\t\n703\t=== 3_1929-08-19_pna_sn82015313_00383349199_1929081901_0244.json\n704\tThe Indianapolis times. [volume] (Indianapolis [Ind.]) 1922-1965 · 1929-08-19\n705\tcrops: None\n706\theadline: HOLLYWOOD HAS\n707\t\n708\t\n709\tEXTRA SHARE OF\n710\t\n711\t\n712\tTRAGEDY HOMES\n713\t\n714\tSiqhtSeers Directed to\n715\tMansions Haunted by\n716\t\n717\t\n718\tBroken Careers.\n719\t---\n720\tBJy Times Special\n721\t\n722\t\n723\tHOLLYWOOD, Cal. Aug. 10. -\n724\tEven as American cities go, Holly\n725\twood is still a boom town, grown\n726\tUP in twenty years from a few scat\n727\ttered farm houses to city known\n728\tin the far corners of the world\n729\tBut for all its youth, Hollywood\n730\talready has more than its share of\n731\ttragedy houses, mansions haunted\n732\twith memories Of vivid careers shat\n733\ttered by scandal and homes closed\n734\tby violent death.\n735\t\n736\t\n737\tEvery town has at least one such\n738\thouse around which dramatic tales\n739\tare woven, but the Hollywood sight\n740\tseer nowadays is directed to fully\n741\ta score of them, and every one has\n742\tits story eerie or sad, notes a cor\n743\trespondent for Photoplay magazine.\n744\t\n745\t\n746\tRudolph Valentines palatial\n747\thome, Falcons Lair, perched high\n748\ton the ledge of a mountain, is still\n749\tthe chief point of interest for the\n750\tmorbidly curious, for it has never\n751\tbeen occupied since the untimely\n752\tdeath of its master. Stripped Of its\n753\tfurnishings and isolated from town,\n754\tit mas taken on a bleak look that\n755\tgives substance to the irresponsible\n756\tlegends of weird noises and panic\n757\tstricken caretakers which have\n758\tgrown up around it.\n759\t\n760\t\n761\tBY contrast, there is the little\n762\t\n763\t=== 10_1895-04-28_pna_sn90059522_00206536822_1895042801_0618.json\n764\tSt. Paul daily globe. [volume] (Saint Paul, Minn.) 1884-1896 · 1895-04-28\n765\tcrops: None\n766\theadline: OVER ONE HUNDRED DEATHS\n767\t\n768\tSaid to Have Occurred Within\n769\tthe Walls Of the Old\n770\t\n771\t\n772\tPlace.\n773\t\n774\tIS THE DWELLING HAUNTED?\n775\t\n776\tThe Good People Of the An\n777\tcient Qu