{"parentUuid":"0136f549-a59d-441f-a2d8-9fd74bfc855f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cga1i6RYAtBVf7itfZWEx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018rsTSubeMrYZQFJUMGHNJJ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Blind second-pass labels, packet 01","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are a second, independent labeller for a newspaper-archive gold set (\"Paper Ghosts\"). Label 30 historical newspaper articles under a written policy, from the article text alone. Work blind: your labels will be compared with another labeller's, so form your own judgement from the policy and the text.\n\nPaths (P is your packet number, 01):\n- Repo root: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\n- Policy: <repo>/eval/gold/POLICY.md. Read all of it before labelling. It defines the six kinds, 19 rules for hard cases, the fields for reports, the four outcomes, the story-place rule and the label record.\n- Your packet: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/packet01.txt. It holds 30 articles. Each starts with \"=== <article_id>\", then \"paper · date\", then a \"crops:\" line (a list of local .jpg paths of the scanned article, or a reason there is none), then \"headline:\", a \"---\" line and the OCR text.\n- Your texts file, for the check: .../scratchpad/p2/texts01.json\n- Your output: .../scratchpad/p2/out/p01.jsonl\n- A work folder for any helper script: .../scratchpad/p2/work/p01/\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Read POLICY.md in full.\n2. For each article, read its text. Where the OCR is unclear, Read its crop images (local files listed on the crops: line), as the policy says. Decide its one kind under the policy's rules. For a report, fill the fields the text states.\n3. Write one JSON object per line, one per article, all 30, with exactly these keys:\n   article_id, kind, kind_quote, place, place_state, seen, outcome, specific_place, place_type, precision, people, rules, slices, crop_used, note\n   - kind: one of report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other. kind_quote is the span of text that shows the kind.\n   - place, place_state, seen, outcome, specific_place, place_type, precision: each null, or {\"value\": \"...\", \"quote\": \"...\"}. people: a list of {\"value\": \"...\", \"quote\": \"...\"} (empty if none).\n   - Fields are for reports only. For any other kind, every field is null and people is [].\n   - Every quote must be an exact span of the article's headline plus OCR text, copied with its OCR errors. Line breaks and runs of spaces may be written as single spaces. Use the shortest span that states the value. A value the text doesn't state stays null; never infer one.\n   - Allowed values: outcome is explained, hoax, unexplained or unknown. place_type is house, church, cemetery, inn_or_hotel, road_or_bridge, public_building, ship or other. precision is town, street or building.\n   - rules: the numbers of the policy's rules you applied. slices: the policy's edge-case codes that fit (E1 to E14, never E9). crop_used: true if you needed a crop. note: one short line; say \"merged\" or \"unreadable\" where the policy asks.\n4. Check: from the repo root run\n   uv run python scripts/second_pass.py check /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/out/p01.jsonl /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/texts01.json\n   It must print \"every label passes checked()\". Fix each error it names and run it again until it does. Also confirm that each of the packet's 30 article ids appears exactly once in your output.\n\nBlindness and safety rules:\n- Open only POLICY.md, your packet, the crop images your packet lists, your texts file, your work folder and your output file.\n- Do not open, list or search anything else in the repo or the scratchpad. In particular, do not open eval/gold/labels.jsonl, eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl, eval/gold/split.json, anything under eval/results or Docs, the scratchpad's labels/ or c1/ folders, or other packets and outputs. Do not read git history.\n- No network access of any kind. Do not run any other script in the repo; the check command above is the only one.\n- Never print, read or echo the repo's .env file.\n- Don't wait for or coordinate with other labellers.\n\nYour final reply, under 120 words: the output path, the count of labels by kind, and each article where you hesitated between two kinds (id, the two kinds, and a few words why).","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1830,"cache_read_input_tokens":466522,"output_tokens":19497,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":34},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1830,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":19497,"cache_read_input_tokens":466522,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1830},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018rsTSubeMrYZQFJUMGHNJJ":{"description":"Blind second-pass labels, packet 01","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"You are a second, independent labeller for a newspaper-archive gold set (\"Paper Ghosts\"). Label 30 historical newspaper articles under a written policy, from the article text alone. Work blind: your labels will be compared with another labeller's, so form your own judgement from the policy and the text.\n\nPaths (P is your packet number, 01):\n- Repo root: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\n- Policy: <repo>/eval/gold/POLICY.md. Read all of it before labelling. It defines the six kinds, 19 rules for hard cases, the fields for reports, the four outcomes, the story-place rule and the label record.\n- Your packet: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/packet01.txt. It holds 30 articles. Each starts with \"=== <article_id>\", then \"paper · date\", then a \"crops:\" line (a list of local .jpg paths of the scanned article, or a reason there is none), then \"headline:\", a \"---\" line and the OCR text.\n- Your texts file, for the check: .../scratchpad/p2/texts01.json\n- Your output: .../scratchpad/p2/out/p01.jsonl\n- A work folder for any helper script: .../scratchpad/p2/work/p01/\n\nWhat to do:\n1. Read POLICY.md in full.\n2. For each article, read its text. Where the OCR is unclear, Read its crop images (local files listed on the crops: line), as the policy says. Decide its one kind under the policy's rules. For a report, fill the fields the text states.\n3. Write one JSON object per line, one per article, all 30, with exactly these keys:\n   article_id, kind, kind_quote, place, place_state, seen, outcome, specific_place, place_type, precision, people, rules, slices, crop_used, note\n   - kind: one of report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other. kind_quote is the span of text that shows the kind.\n   - place, place_state, seen, outcome, specific_place, place_type, precision: each null, or {\"value\": \"...\", \"quote\": \"...\"}. people: a list of {\"value\": \"...\", \"quote\": \"...\"} (empty if none).\n   - Fields are for reports only. For any other kind, every field is null and people is [].\n   - Every quote must be an exact span of the article's headline plus OCR text, copied with its OCR errors. Line breaks and runs of spaces may be written as single spaces. Use the shortest span that states the value. A value the text doesn't state stays null; never infer one.\n   - Allowed values: outcome is explained, hoax, unexplained or unknown. place_type is house, church, cemetery, inn_or_hotel, road_or_bridge, public_building, ship or other. precision is town, street or building.\n   - rules: the numbers of the policy's rules you applied. slices: the policy's edge-case codes that fit (E1 to E14, never E9). crop_used: true if you needed a crop. note: one short line; say \"merged\" or \"unreadable\" where the policy asks.\n4. Check: from the repo root run\n   uv run python scripts/second_pass.py check /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/out/p01.jsonl /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/p2/texts01.json\n   It must print \"every label passes checked()\". Fix each error it names and run it again until it does. Also confirm that each of the packet's 30 article ids appears exactly once in your output.\n\nBlindness and safety rules:\n- Open only POLICY.md, your packet, the crop images your packet lists, your texts file, your work folder and your output file.\n- Do not open, list or search anything else in the repo or the scratchpad. In particular, do not open eval/gold/labels.jsonl, eval/gold/dev_labels.jsonl, eval/gold/split.json, anything under eval/results or Docs, the scratchpad's labels/ or c1/ folders, or other packets and outputs. Do not read git history.\n- No network access of any kind. Do not run any other script in the repo; the check command above is the only one.\n- Never print, read or echo the repo's .env file.\n- Don't wait for or coordinate with other labellers.\n\nYour final reply, under 120 words: the output path, the count