{"parentUuid":"a4a7cce8-6304-4ece-8582-1c094e614443","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cga2Wz9qCWk5nhAP6eEWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"One output has appeared (packet 10). While the rest finish, I'm drafting decision 38's narrative in scratch."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_read_input_tokens":551702,"output_tokens":2929,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":925},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3166,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":551702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3166},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2b5b237b-9ed7-460d-86dc-a1bb2696b170","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cga2WyZc2DzdrQjeD5Jtg","requestRef":"d9c47d3b-c704-4088-aa15-cd1a4fe249bd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"be551884-3172-4d11-8c28-97c96a2a98f1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:49:35.209Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"be551884-3172-4d11-8c28-97c96a2a98f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cga2Wz9qCWk5nhAP6eEWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0175TcPuQ4eEuUCLy3e4hUSF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/d38_draft.md","content":"**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md` v2, all 450, each through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev, and agrees with the first on {{KIND_AGREE}} of kinds (κ {{KAPPA}}). Every disagreement is ruled on under `POLICY.md`, both labels kept, and the labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output exists. Gold holds {{REPORTS}} reports, against the 35.3 expected.**\n\n- **The first pass:** I labelled all 300 gold and 150 dev articles in batches of 20, in the page's seeded order, with no stratum or weight in view, and committed each batch as I went.\n  - Every label passes `checked()`: its kind is one of `POLICY.md`'s, its fields are a report's only, every value has its quote, every quote is in the text, and every choice is the schema's.\n  - Gold: 45 reports, 89 other, 68 fiction, 59 idiom, 28 adverts, 11 religious. Dev: 32 reports, 44 other, 31 fiction, 26 idiom, 10 adverts, 7 religious.\n  - **Crops:** 443 of the 450 articles have them, cached one at a time at loc.gov's pace. The other 7 fail the page check or have too few words to check. I read the crop wherever the OCR was unclear, 7 times in gold and 9 in dev. Eight dev labels were made before their crops arrived, so I read those crops afterwards and mended the labels.\n- **The calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller**, applied the same way in gold and dev:\n  - An apparition of the living is a report when a figure is seen, as for Buller's sight of Wolseley.\n  - An essay or sermon that tells several particular claims takes its fields from the first told in particulars: Scott's sight of the dead Byron in the Westminster Review's essay on hallucinations, and Slade's slate-writing in the Boston Pilot's round-up of exposures.\n  - A column of short items under one heading is one article. Rule 16 and E11 are kept for segmentation errors: an article's tail, or an advert, joined to another.\n  - E1 is the religious kind's Holy Ghost. A joke's catechism or a pioneer tale's blazes are not E1.\n  - E3 marks fiction whose plot holds a ghost, sham or real. A ghost used as a figure in a poem or story is not E3.\n  - A place's state comes only from the text or the dateline. \"Abba. la\" is read as Albia, Ia., the dateline the crop shows. New York as a city gives no state.\n- **The blind second pass** (`scripts/second_pass.py`): 330 articles, all of gold and 30 of dev, drawn with the seed \"2C.2 second pass dev sample\".\n  - 11 reading agents each took a packet of 30, in one seeded shuffle across the two splits, so no packet shows which split an article is from.\n  - Each saw only its packet, the crops it lists, and `POLICY.md`: no first label, stratum, weight or split. Each was barred from the label files, the split, the results, the docs and git history.\n  - Each checked its labels with `second_pass.py check`, which runs `checked()` against its packet's texts alone. Then I checked and saved them all through `label_gold.py`, as labeller `second pass`.\n- **Agreement, before any ruling** (`eval/results/phase2c/agreement.json`), with 95% intervals: Wilson for each rate, a bootstrap of 2,000 resamples for κ.\n\n{{AGREEMENT_TABLE}}\n\n  - A field agrees when both leave it empty, or when the values match for the choices and the state. For place, seen and the specific place, the quotes must overlap in the text, or the values match. For people, each person must overlap one of the other pass's, both ways.\n\n{{FIELD_TABLE}}\n\n- **The rulings:** {{DISPUTES}} articles disagreed, {{KIND_DISPUTES}} on kind and {{FIELD_DISPUTES}} on fields alone. Each has a `ruling` record beside both labels, whose note gives the reason. The final label is the ruling where there is one, else the first pass's (`gold_measures.final`).\n\n{{RULING_SUMMARY}}\n\n- **The freeze:** `eval/gold/HASH` lists the sha256 of `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` beside `split.json`'s, committed at {{FREEZE_COMMIT}}, before any model output. `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.\n- **Gold's reports by stratum** (`eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`), beside the draw's expectation:\n\n{{STRATUM_TABLE}}\n\n- **The weighted report rate:** {{WEIGHTED}}.\n- **The story-place rule, as code** (`gold_measures.story_state`). It takes a state named after a comma in the place's quote; else a town of the quote named elsewhere with a state; else the dateline's. It never takes the paper's.\n\n{{PLACE_RESULT}}\n\n- **Slices:** {{SLICES}}\n- **The grouping missed one reprint within gold:** the comic sketch of a backwoods preacher is printed twice in gold. Two printings within gold don't leak into training. Each is labelled alone and agrees with the other.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_read_input_tokens":551702,"output_tokens":2929,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":925},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3166,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2929,"cache_read_input_tokens":551702,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3166,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3166},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0175TcPuQ4eEuUCLy3e4hUSF":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/d38_draft.md","content":"**38. Gold and dev are labelled by hand under `POLICY.md` v2, all 450, each through the page's `checked()`. A blind second pass relabels all of gold and a seeded fifth of dev, and agrees with the first on {{KIND_AGREE}} of kinds (κ {{KAPPA}}). Every disagreement is ruled on under `POLICY.md`, both labels kept, and the labels are frozen by sha256 before any model output exists. Gold holds {{REPORTS}} reports, against the 35.3 expected.**\n\n- **The first pass:** I labelled all 300 gold and 150 dev articles in batches of 20, in the page's seeded order, with no stratum or weight in view, and committed each batch as I went.\n  - Every label passes `checked()`: its kind is one of `POLICY.md`'s, its fields are a report's only, every value has its quote, every quote is in the text, and every choice is the schema's.\n  - Gold: 45 reports, 89 other, 68 fiction, 59 idiom, 28 adverts, 11 religious. Dev: 32 reports, 44 other, 31 fiction, 26 idiom, 10 adverts, 7 religious.\n  - **Crops:** 443 of the 450 articles have them, cached one at a time at loc.gov's pace. The other 7 fail the page check or have too few words to check. I read the crop wherever the OCR was unclear, 7 times in gold and 9 in dev. Eight dev labels were made before their crops arrived, so I read those crops afterwards and mended the labels.\n- **The calls `POLICY.md` left to the labeller**, applied the same way in gold and dev:\n  - An apparition of the living is a report when a figure is seen, as for Buller's sight of Wolseley.\n  - An essay or sermon that tells several particular claims takes its fields from the first told in particulars: Scott's sight of the dead Byron in the Westminster Review's essay on hallucinations, and Slade's slate-writing in the Boston Pilot's round-up of exposures.\n  - A column of short items under one heading is one article. Rule 16 and E11 are kept for segmentation errors: an article's tail, or an advert, joined to another.\n  - E1 is the religious kind's Holy Ghost. A joke's catechism or a pioneer tale's blazes are not E1.\n  - E3 marks fiction whose plot holds a ghost, sham or real. A ghost used as a figure in a poem or story is not E3.\n  - A place's state comes only from the text or the dateline. \"Abba. la\" is read as Albia, Ia., the dateline the crop shows. New York as a city gives no state.\n- **The blind second pass** (`scripts/second_pass.py`): 330 articles, all of gold and 30 of dev, drawn with the seed \"2C.2 second pass dev sample\".\n  - 11 reading agents each took a packet of 30, in one seeded shuffle across the two splits, so no packet shows which split an article is from.\n  - Each saw only its packet, the crops it lists, and `POLICY.md`: no first label, stratum, weight or split. Each was barred from the label files, the split, the results, the docs and git history.\n  - Each checked its labels with `second_pass.py check`, which runs `checked()` against its packet's texts alone. Then I checked and saved them all through `label_gold.py`, as labeller `second pass`.\n- **Agreement, before any ruling** (`eval/results/phase2c/agreement.json`), with 95% intervals: Wilson for each rate, a bootstrap of 2,000 resamples for κ.\n\n{{AGREEMENT_TABLE}}\n\n  - A field agrees when both leave it empty, or when the values match for the choices and the state. For place, seen and the specific place, the quotes must overlap in the text, or the values match. For people, each person must overlap one of the other pass's, both ways.\n\n{{FIELD_TABLE}}\n\n- **The rulings:** {{DISPUTES}} articles disagreed, {{KIND_DISPUTES}} on kind and {{FIELD_DISPUTES}} on fields alone. Each has a `ruling` record beside both labels, whose note gives the reason. The final label is the ruling where there is one, else the first pass's (`gold_measures.final`).\n\n{{RULING_SUMMARY}}\n\n- **The freeze:** `eval/gold/HASH` lists the sha256 of `labels.jsonl` and `dev_labels.jsonl` beside `split.json`'s, committed at {{FREEZE_COMMIT}}, before any model output. `check_leakage.py` now checks every file `HASH` lists.\n- **Gold's reports by stratum** (`eval/results/phase2c/gold_measures.json`), beside the draw's expectation:\n\n{{STRATUM_TABLE}}\n\n- **The weighted report rate:** {{WEIGHTED}}.\n- **The story-place rule, as code** (`gold_measures.story_state`). It takes a state named after a comma in the place's quote; else a town of the quote named elsewhere with a state; else the dateline's. It never takes the paper's.\n\n{{PLACE_RESULT}}\n\n- **Slices:** {{SLICES}}\n- **The grouping missed one reprint within gold:** the comic sketch of a backwoods preacher is printed twice in gold. Two printings within gold don't leak into training. Each is labelled alone and agrees with the other.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2b5b237b-9ed7-460d-86dc-a1bb2696b170","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cga2WyZc2DzdrQjeD5Jtg","requestRef":"d9c47d3b-c704-4088-aa15-cd1a4fe249bd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e5e2f97e-a719-48bc-a3ba-87a8ce651e45","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:49:52.896Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
