{"parentUuid":"c523439b-5b25-4a3a-bcf2-287fd05ebc6f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"775e54ef-6487-4f79-8598-643421b87718","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GGnACv4wHTNbb75VjrqVci","type":"tool_result","content":"every label passes checked()\nevery label passes checked()\n      20\n##### 0: 10_1878-03-07_p4_sn84027691_0023728334A_1878030701_0641.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['people']\n=== 10_1878-03-07_p4_sn84027691_0023728334A_1878030701_0641.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/48c8478f6d78b48471fbdbb8.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/5f431e961853554ae13a8d79.jpg']\nheadline: \n---\na SsaFsling ltssle Episode which n\n\n\nclaAes . Real Ghess-Fact, and n0s\n\n\nFicsioa.\n\n\nThis is a real ghost story which is about\nto be related, an actual occurrence, founded\non stern facts, the work of neither disor-\ndered fancy, wild imagination nor overbur-\ndened stomach, but something which act\nually transp;red, and, while the reporter\ndid not hear it from the actual participator\nin the ghos.ly seance, he has it from au-\nthority which is unimpeachable. Some\ntune ago, and not 90 long = time either, q\nlady from the East was visiting at the resi-\ndsnce of q well-known family here. The\nAforesaid residence is not haunted, at least\nnever was before, Its visitants having always\nbeen of the real flesh and blood order, and\nNO spiritual manifestations having ever\ntaken place there before. 1t was in\n\n\nTHE DEAD OF NIGHT,\n\n\nthat time VIXEN ghosts and spirits most like\nto provl, when this beautiful vision appear\ned. 1t vas none Of your skull and crosl\nbone kind, but lovely lady dressed in the\nheight Of fashion (ghoss fashion oi\noourse) as though just having\ncone from . ball a party givsa,\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This is a real ghost story which is about to be related\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"printed as fact; a visiting lady sees a fashionable lady's ghost at night; cut off in the archive\",\n \"place\": \"a well-known family's residence  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a lovely lady dressed in the height of fashion  <<lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<as though just having cone from . ball a party givsa>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the family's residence  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"a lady from the East  <<q lady from the East>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This is a real ghost story which is about to be related, an actual occurrence\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"framed as fact on unimpeachable authority, not as a tale; text breaks off mid-account\",\n \"place\": \"the residence of a well-known family here  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a beautiful vision of a lovely lady dressed in the height of fashion  <<lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<1t vas none Of your skull and crosl bone kind, but lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion (ghoss fashion oi oourse) as though just having cone from . ball a party givsa>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the residence of a well-known family  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<Aforesaid residence>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"the actual participator in the ghostly seance  <<the actual participator in the ghos.ly seance>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 1: 1_1896-07-06_p14_sn85066387_0017503741A_1896070601_0113.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['place_type']\n=== 1_1896-07-06_p14_sn85066387_0017503741A_1896070601_0113.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/d0057a1f64e61dd90ba08b93.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/399d75952ad6c6a275f8b6c6.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2d4f1ccd58be6555cb0f9dec.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/129a998d40ad81b89d008c0a.jpg']\nheadline: She Wants to Join Her Husband\nin the Spirit Land When\n\n\nUnder Them.\n\nIS NOW IN A PADDED CELL\n\nThe Doctors at the Receiving Hos.\npital Can See No Signs of In.\n\n\nsanity in Her.\n---\nThe case of Mrs. Allie Gender, widow\n53 years of age, will form subject for in\nvestigation by the Insanity Commission\ners this morning.\n\n\nShe is in padded cell in the Receiving\nHospital charged with insanity, but any\none who talks with her cannot see the\nslightest sign OF mental alteration in hel\nconduct or speech. Yet her friends say\nshe is crazy, and too dangerous to be al\nlarge.\n\n\nTwelve years ago her husband was killed\nin railroad accident. He had an accl-\ndent policy for $500, and this sum was\npaid to the widow. or rather to Albert\nShainwald, her brother-in-law, living at\n207 Geary street, who was administrator Of\nher husbands estate.\n\n\nThe widow was left with three young\nchildren, boy and two girls. They were\nput in home and the mother worked\nhard to support herself and them. The\n$500 was placed on deposit in the San\nFrancisco Savings Union bank and with\ninterest it has reached the sum of $2100. OF\nthis amount $500 has been withdrawn and\nloaned to G. Petrie, printer in Alameda.\n\n\nMrs. Gender about two years ago went\nto live with her brother-in-law, but three\nweeks ago she removed to 238 Sixth street,\nwhere she engaged a room. According TO\nthe landlady, Mrs. George, she showed\nsymptoms of insanity shortly after being\nin her house and on Saturday she became\nviolent and threatened to take her life, so\nDR.. Bohm was sent for and he ordered\nthat she be sent to the Receiving Hospital.\n\n\nHer chief hallucination is that her hus-\nbands spirit is constantly with her.\nWhen walking on the street she imagined\nhat har hnos do J., II\nverse with him as if he were in the flesh\nat night she would alarm every one in\nthe house by going from room to room\nsearching for her husband and when she\ncould not find him she became violent and\nhad to be placed under restraint.\n\n\nWhen she became calm she would talk\nnationally and say she wanted to Join her\nhusband in the spirit land and if the\nmoney was only divided among her chill\ndren she would soon be with him.\n\n\nThe Oldest, young man % years of age,\nis in Mendocino County, where he has\nbought some Government land. One of\nthe girls is married and the other is a\nservant with family on Union street.\nApparently the money is not to be di-\nvided till the youngest. who is now 20\n| years of age. attains the age of 2i.\n| Speaking of her arrest Mrs. Gender said\nyesterday: sl think it is all a Joke to\nkeep me here. was in my room vester.\nday when two men wearing blue uniforms\ncame and asked me to put on my shoe.\nand come with them. Then they put me\nin patrol wagon and brought me here\n| But | don't know why. l am not crazy\nand | cannot see why l should be kept\nhere\"\n\n\nThe doctors at the hospital who have\nconversed with her say that she does not\nexhibit the slightest symptoms of in.\nsanity, but the landlord and landlady o.\nthe lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street, DR.\nBohm and others say that she has spells\nand when under them she is violently\n/ insane.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"bands spirit is constantly with her\",\n \"rules\": [\n  2,\n  3\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a widow's hallucination of her dead husband's spirit, before an insanity commission\",\n \"place\": \"238 Sixth Street  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"seen\": \"her dead husband's spirit constantly with her  <<bands spirit is constantly with her>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"explained  <<Her chief hallucination>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"inn_or_hotel  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Mrs. Allie Gender  <<Mrs. Allie Gender>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"Her chief hallucination is that her hus- bands spirit is constantly with her.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  2,\n  3\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"insanity case; the felt presence of her dead husband is called a hallucination\",\n \"place\": \"238 Sixth Street  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"seen\": \"her husband's spirit constantly with her  <<her hus- bands spirit is constantly with her>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"explained  <<Her chief hallucination>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street  <<lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<lodging-house>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Mrs. Allie Gender  <<Mrs. Allie Gender>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 2: 20_1879-04-11_pna_sn83032041_00212477710_1879041101_0201.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['seen']\n=== 20_1879-04-11_pna_sn83032041_00212477710_1879041101_0201.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f642f18b09e871d4da8bd52d.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/54f207c0d773976b42ca1f82.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f3b9a02de861bff2f7081e3f.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2d9adca2e7e37842d40cfec5.jpg']\nheadline: \"THE HAUNTED HOUSE,\n\n4 Strange hut True story Related by\n\n\nDan J. Garrity i'm Boston Pilot.\n---\nThe time OF my narrative dates back\nto the year 1870. The events occurred\nin the city of Springfield. Ohio.\n\n\nSituated in the very centre of the city\nwas a mansion. old and lonely in aspect.\nthe property of a Mr.. FoOs. 1t had been\nfor several years Uninhabited. when\nstrange reports began to circulate Per\nsons who passed there at midnight, and\nother uncanny hours, often saw strange\nlights and heard stranger sounds, until\npeople believed that it was haunted.\n\n\nAt length two young men of the town\nresolved to see whether it was haunted\nor not, and thus put the fears and gOS-\nsipings of the towns people to an end.\n\n\nAccordingly they took up their quar-\ntiers at the mansion. About eight\nO'Clock they lit their candles, and made\nthemselves comfortable to receive their\nghoStly visitors.\n\n\nThe clock struck nine, ten, eleven. and\nit was now nearly twelve O'Clock. the\ntime for ghosts to appear. The great\nclock in st. Raphael's church began to\nstrike one. two, three. four, five, six.\nseven, eight. nine, ten, eleven, t,reIre.\nand then-No sooner had the sOnorous\npeals died away. than the candles were\nsuddenly OXtnguiShed. and they were\nleft in darkness. After a few minutes\nbright. circular light became visible\nnear one of the walls, and what terrible\nspectacle was brought to view \\ man\nwas stretched from tree with a rope\naround his neck. while a box lay at his\nfeet within reach-he was a suicide\n/ His distorted features and glaring eyes\nwere plainly visible, while his tongue.\nblack and swollen. hung at least half a\nfoot from his month To complete the\nhorrible picture. hundreds of demons\ntod\nThen followed wild burst of laughter\nand the apparition vanished.\nThe young men had not expected this.\nWhile this strange scene was enactmg\nthey sat stUpefied with fear, their hair\nactually standing on end.\n\n\nAt length their horrible spell was\nbroken, and without even stopping to\nsnatch their hats, they fled the house\nAs they were fleeing along the street.\nthey ran right into the arms of tall,\nmuScUlaTman, who seeing their alright\ned condition. frightened his grasp upon\nthem, and asked them to explain their\nfright.\n\n\nThey told him all.\n\n\nAfter they had finished their story,\nthe detective for it was no other than\nDetective John Burnside. of New \\ Ork.\nwho was visiting friends there told\nthem Ito say nothing about it, but wait\nand hope and he would discover the\nmystery if possible\n\n\nAbout two weeks after the detective\nreturned hOme-so his friends thought.\n\n\nIn course of time the young men dis\ncovered that they conld no longer keep\nthe secret. and 50 they divulged it.\n\n\n1t raised great excitement, of course,\nand the people Of the city gave the place\na wide berth.\n\n\nThe strange sounds and sights We're\ncontinued. until the people believed\nwithout a doubt that the house was\nhaunted.\n\n\nWe Will pass over year.\n\n\nOne morning a posse of police, headed\nby Il tall man in plain clothes, approach\ned the FuOs mansion. unlocked the door,\nand passed in.\n\n\nIn a few minutes the sound of pistol\nShots was heard. and then all was still.\nIn few minutes the posse emerged from\nthe house. looking much larger. What\ncould il mean\n\n\nAnd now, little Ants. my narrative is\nat an end, and Detective Burnside will\nfinish the story.\n\n\nNARRATIVE by DETECTIVE BURN\n\n\nSIDE.\n\n\nAfter | left the two young men, said\nDetective Burnside afterwards in telling\nthe story. my mind was made up\nwould discover the mystery.\n\n\nAccordingly. the next evening. | pro-\nceeded to the mansion. It was a mere\nrepetition OF the story of the young men,\nas far as the apparitiOn. As soon as the\nclock struck twelve my candle was\nblown ont by gust Of wind | know.\ncaused by the slamming of doors. And\nwhat a terrible sight met my eye. |\nshudder now when | think of it, 50 ter\nribly real it looked.\n\n\nThere in the same spot that the young\nmen had described | saw young and\nbeautiful girl on her knees \\ form\nwas bending over her. its hand clas ped\nher long golden hair, while a keen.\nbloody knife was drawn across her fair\nwhite throat, while torrents of crimson\nblood dripped down upon the floor.\n\n\n| regained by self-posseSSion enough tC\ndraw my pistol. aim. and fire. y wild\nlaugh followed. and my bullet was heard\ncrashing through the wainscoting.\nThe apparition vanished slowly. anC\nhappening to turn around discovered\nthe mystery.\n\n\n1t was gang of some sort. / wa:\nsure, and | was resolved to capture\nthem. A few weeks after | joined tn,\ngang. 10y means known only to myself\na professional secret. There were coun\n, terfeiters, burglars. and everything els'\n, among them. I Will not weary the read\n\n\neT with a description of the numerOu\n\n\nburglaTieS they committed. or of the va\n\n\nrious WAYS in which they manufacture,\n= and - showed their queer money\ne After staying with them for about\nt year, | resolved to break up the gang\n2 for l had now ample evidence to convic\nD them.\n\n\ne Accordingly. l obtained the posse q\n+ police. and raided the house. After\ne slight resistance they were captured.\nI When they found out who their cap\n2 tor was they threatened me with ven\nI geance dire, if they ever escaped bu\n+ they never did, for there was not one c\n' them but had committed enough crime\n+ TO condemn them for life.\nIS \\ few weeks after the gang We're sen\n4 to prison ! took opportunity to sho'\nG some visitors the house, and explain tn\nq secret of the ghosts In ther room whel\nV the apparitiOn\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"4 Strange hut True story Related by\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6,\n  7,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"printed as a true story from the Boston Pilot, though told to children; a gang's magic lantern; merged with an item on a shoemaker's stone\",\n \"place\": \"the Foos mansion, Springfield, Ohio  <<in the city of Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Ohio  <<Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a bright circular light, and apparitions of a hanged man and a murdered girl  <<bright. circular light became visible>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<away by means of a magic lantern>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Foos mansion  <<the property of a Mr.. FoOs>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<was a mansion. old and lonely in aspect>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the property of a Mr.. FoOs>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"persons who passed at midnight  <<Per sons who passed there at midnight>>\",\n  \"two young men of the town  <<two young men of the town>>\",\n  \"Detective John Burnside  <<Detective John Burnside>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"until people believed that it was haunted\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6,\n  7,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"merged; signals conflict, the text's own framing ('A Strange but True Story') decides\",\n \"place\": \"Springfield, Ohio  <<the city of Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Ohio  <<Ohio>>\",\n \"seen\": \"strange lights and stranger sounds  <<saw strange lights and heard stranger sounds>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<they frightened thel e away by means of a magic lantern>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Foos mansion  <<the FuOs mansion>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<a mansion>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the FuOs mansion>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"persons who passed there at midnight  <<Per sons who passed there at midnight>>\",\n  \"two young men of the town  <<two young men of the town>>\",\n  \"Detective John Burnside  <<Detective John Burnside>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 3: 22_1914-08-24_pna_sn88085187_00211108381_1914082401_0591.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 22_1914-08-24_pna_sn88085187_00211108381_1914082401_0591.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/dc1cfa0456713bf97ab95035.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/288d846c03b2ae64a034c13f.jpg']\nheadline: The Parental School\n---\nAn inspection of the Parental School, supervised\nby the local school board, forcefuly impresses the\nvisitor that the 20-odd lads confined therein are\nas matter of fact, enjoying vastly better home in\nfluenee than perhaps one-half the boys who live\nwith their parents Mr.. and Mrs. John c. Greene,\nIn charge of the school, young folk. Greene who\nis head -master, farm boss, companion and robust\nvithal is young enough to have the boys viewpoint.\nPersonally If boy again, we would be\nstrongly tempted to hook jack and thrust out an i'm\npudent tongue at the truant officer and devise other\ndevilish means, to enjoy few months at the Parent\nal school, it is conducted in Tacoma. Once boy\nhas been judge \"ineorrigble,' the best way, sane\nauthorities agree, to improve him is to strengthen\nhis spirit, not to break it, 'tIncorrigbty' in boys\nIs another and more awsesome term for BOYS who\nnot milksops. We hazard the guess that Huclxleber\nry Finn, and Teddy Roosevelt and Henry Ford and\nsuch, were \"incorrigibles' in their day.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe direct primary is great advertising medium\nSome of these county candidates may not get any\nvotes, except from their family, but they had\ntheir pictures every fence and tree in the city for\nweeks.\n\n\nTacomas police force is getting desperate 1t be-\ngan Saturday night to arrest motorcycles and auto\nmobiles. Wonder why we don't hear of 'em pinch\ning some of the dives that Mavor Faweett has ex-\nposed and reported to Mills and Loomisg\n\n\nChief of Police Ardella p LOOMS openly defies\nthe mayor to prove charges of graft But he ceverlv\nmentions in his interview that if there is graft in\nthe police department he doesn't know anything\nshout it. The coppers ought to feel gratfied toward\ntheir boss for the inuendo supplied in the statement\n\n\nCongressman johnson doesn't feel that he can\nleave Washington to do a little fenee-budng IN his\ndistrict All of which goes to show that johnson has\nmore sense than believed he had The money\nthat he would spend on the trip and campaign will\ncome IN handy when be retires from congress next\nspring\n\n\narmy EngIand's to get $4,000 dozen American eggs\nat pc the Dozen\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"The direct primary is great advertising medium\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"editorial paragraphs; spirit and medium in their ordinary senses\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"to strengthen his spirit, not to break it\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"merged: editorial paragraphs; spirit and advertising medium in non-ghost senses.\"\n}\n\n##### 4: 29_1909-12-27_pna_sn92053934_00202198764_1909122701_0152.json  kinds=['other', 'advert'] fields=[]\n=== 29_1909-12-27_pna_sn92053934_00202198764_1909122701_0152.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2a06a6cfc26aaf958bb9393c.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/ebfad0e4f1e8d4003e0fbda7.jpg']\nheadline: The Society of Spiritual Truth.\n\n\nFREE! FREE!\n1O4H West Second street.\n---\nSpiritual meeting Sunday evening\nSpirit message demonstrating immortal\nity. Tests will be given. Doors open 7\np. m. Lecture and tests p. m. Ladies\nand gentlemen welcome. Your departed\nspirit friends viii talk to you through\nthe medium. Seats free. No collections.\nLeClaire Hall, Davenport, Iowa\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"Your departed spirit friends viii talk to you through the medium.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  4\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E5\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a society's notice of a meeting with messages, for later\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"advert\",\n \"kq\": \"Seats free. No collections.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  12\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E5\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"spiritualist meeting notice promising messages through a medium\"\n}\n\n##### 5: 2_1909-04-08_p1_sn86058226_00271744729_1909040801_0067.json  kinds=['fiction', 'report'] fields=[]\n=== 2_1909-04-08_p1_sn86058226_00271744729_1909040801_0067.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/69c54811f79a1256e92c34e5.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b1bc059efa8d6e8b1807fbf4.jpg']\nheadline: A Ghost In q Clock.\n---\nBasingstoke provides 4 remarkable\nstory Of ghost in the form Of q clock.\nAt the approach Of midnight each\nnight the otherwise peaceful grand\nfather'' becomes inhabited by 4 spook.\nThe ticking changes into 4 deep and\npeculiar humping, the clock increases\nIn stature. while a pair Of gray feet\nprotrude from beneath its base. Pass\ning through transitional stages the\nhumping il replaced by q spasmodic\nbreathing. and upon the stroke OF IL\nthe pendulum door opens, revealing an\nenormous ashy gray hand with NAL.\nshaped fingers. The clock face dis\nappears, displaying q frightful gray\nhead. large and round, with abnormal.\n\" long. pale blue eyes. Beyond a\nquiet stroll. which causes weird tap\npings along the landings during the\nnight. the appariticn il inolfensive and\nis said to prove Of great service In\nsending every one early to bed.-Lon-\ndon Tit Bits.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"fiction\",\n \"kq\": \"Ghost In q Clock.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  8\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E7\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a Tit-Bits jest about a haunted clock at Basingstoke\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"Basingstoke provides 4 remarkable story Of ghost in the form Of q clock.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  8,\n  14\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E7\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"Tit-Bits paragraph on a haunted clock at Basingstoke, told as a local story with a closing quip.\",\n \"place\": \"Basingstoke  <<Basingstoke>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a ghost in the form of a grandfather clock: thumping, gray feet, an ashy gray hand and a gray head  <<ghost in the form Of q clock>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<Beyond a quiet stroll. which causes weird tap pings along the landings during the night. the appariticn il inolfensive and is said to prove Of great service In sending every one early to bed.>>\",\n \"precision\": \"town  <<Basingstoke>>\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0e270a44-5d32-4478-9d8b-f544c42efb18","timestamp":"2026-10-31T08:50:55.807Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"every label passes checked()\nevery label passes checked()\n      20\n##### 0: 10_1878-03-07_p4_sn84027691_0023728334A_1878030701_0641.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['people']\n=== 10_1878-03-07_p4_sn84027691_0023728334A_1878030701_0641.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/48c8478f6d78b48471fbdbb8.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/5f431e961853554ae13a8d79.jpg']\nheadline: \n---\na SsaFsling ltssle Episode which n\n\n\nclaAes . Real Ghess-Fact, and n0s\n\n\nFicsioa.\n\n\nThis is a real ghost story which is about\nto be related, an actual occurrence, founded\non stern facts, the work of neither disor-\ndered fancy, wild imagination nor overbur-\ndened stomach, but something which act\nually transp;red, and, while the reporter\ndid not hear it from the actual participator\nin the ghos.ly seance, he has it from au-\nthority which is unimpeachable. Some\ntune ago, and not 90 long = time either, q\nlady from the East was visiting at the resi-\ndsnce of q well-known family here. The\nAforesaid residence is not haunted, at least\nnever was before, Its visitants having always\nbeen of the real flesh and blood order, and\nNO spiritual manifestations having ever\ntaken place there before. 1t was in\n\n\nTHE DEAD OF NIGHT,\n\n\nthat time VIXEN ghosts and spirits most like\nto provl, when this beautiful vision appear\ned. 1t vas none Of your skull and crosl\nbone kind, but lovely lady dressed in the\nheight Of fashion (ghoss fashion oi\noourse) as though just having\ncone from . ball a party givsa,\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This is a real ghost story which is about to be related\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"printed as fact; a visiting lady sees a fashionable lady's ghost at night; cut off in the archive\",\n \"place\": \"a well-known family's residence  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a lovely lady dressed in the height of fashion  <<lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<as though just having cone from . ball a party givsa>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the family's residence  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"a lady from the East  <<q lady from the East>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This is a real ghost story which is about to be related, an actual occurrence\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"framed as fact on unimpeachable authority, not as a tale; text breaks off mid-account\",\n \"place\": \"the residence of a well-known family here  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family here>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a beautiful vision of a lovely lady dressed in the height of fashion  <<lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<1t vas none Of your skull and crosl bone kind, but lovely lady dressed in the height Of fashion (ghoss fashion oi oourse) as though just having cone from . ball a party givsa>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the residence of a well-known family  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<Aforesaid residence>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the resi- dsnce of q well-known family>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"the actual participator in the ghostly seance  <<the actual participator in the ghos.ly seance>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 1: 1_1896-07-06_p14_sn85066387_0017503741A_1896070601_0113.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['place_type']\n=== 1_1896-07-06_p14_sn85066387_0017503741A_1896070601_0113.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/d0057a1f64e61dd90ba08b93.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/399d75952ad6c6a275f8b6c6.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2d4f1ccd58be6555cb0f9dec.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/129a998d40ad81b89d008c0a.jpg']\nheadline: She Wants to Join Her Husband\nin the Spirit Land When\n\n\nUnder Them.\n\nIS NOW IN A PADDED CELL\n\nThe Doctors at the Receiving Hos.\npital Can See No Signs of In.\n\n\nsanity in Her.\n---\nThe case of Mrs. Allie Gender, widow\n53 years of age, will form subject for in\nvestigation by the Insanity Commission\ners this morning.\n\n\nShe is in padded cell in the Receiving\nHospital charged with insanity, but any\none who talks with her cannot see the\nslightest sign OF mental alteration in hel\nconduct or speech. Yet her friends say\nshe is crazy, and too dangerous to be al\nlarge.\n\n\nTwelve years ago her husband was killed\nin railroad accident. He had an accl-\ndent policy for $500, and this sum was\npaid to the widow. or rather to Albert\nShainwald, her brother-in-law, living at\n207 Geary street, who was administrator Of\nher husbands estate.\n\n\nThe widow was left with three young\nchildren, boy and two girls. They were\nput in home and the mother worked\nhard to support herself and them. The\n$500 was placed on deposit in the San\nFrancisco Savings Union bank and with\ninterest it has reached the sum of $2100. OF\nthis amount $500 has been withdrawn and\nloaned to G. Petrie, printer in Alameda.\n\n\nMrs. Gender about two years ago went\nto live with her brother-in-law, but three\nweeks ago she removed to 238 Sixth street,\nwhere she engaged a room. According TO\nthe landlady, Mrs. George, she showed\nsymptoms of insanity shortly after being\nin her house and on Saturday she became\nviolent and threatened to take her life, so\nDR.. Bohm was sent for and he ordered\nthat she be sent to the Receiving Hospital.\n\n\nHer chief hallucination is that her hus-\nbands spirit is constantly with her.\nWhen walking on the street she imagined\nhat har hnos do J., II\nverse with him as if he were in the flesh\nat night she would alarm every one in\nthe house by going from room to room\nsearching for her husband and when she\ncould not find him she became violent and\nhad to be placed under restraint.\n\n\nWhen she became calm she would talk\nnationally and say she wanted to Join her\nhusband in the spirit land and if the\nmoney was only divided among her chill\ndren she would soon be with him.\n\n\nThe Oldest, young man % years of age,\nis in Mendocino County, where he has\nbought some Government land. One of\nthe girls is married and the other is a\nservant with family on Union street.\nApparently the money is not to be di-\nvided till the youngest. who is now 20\n| years of age. attains the age of 2i.\n| Speaking of her arrest Mrs. Gender said\nyesterday: sl think it is all a Joke to\nkeep me here. was in my room vester.\nday when two men wearing blue uniforms\ncame and asked me to put on my shoe.\nand come with them. Then they put me\nin patrol wagon and brought me here\n| But | don't know why. l am not crazy\nand | cannot see why l should be kept\nhere\"\n\n\nThe doctors at the hospital who have\nconversed with her say that she does not\nexhibit the slightest symptoms of in.\nsanity, but the landlord and landlady o.\nthe lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street, DR.\nBohm and others say that she has spells\nand when under them she is violently\n/ insane.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"bands spirit is constantly with her\",\n \"rules\": [\n  2,\n  3\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a widow's hallucination of her dead husband's spirit, before an insanity commission\",\n \"place\": \"238 Sixth Street  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"seen\": \"her dead husband's spirit constantly with her  <<bands spirit is constantly with her>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"explained  <<Her chief hallucination>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"inn_or_hotel  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Mrs. Allie Gender  <<Mrs. Allie Gender>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"Her chief hallucination is that her hus- bands spirit is constantly with her.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  2,\n  3\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"insanity case; the felt presence of her dead husband is called a hallucination\",\n \"place\": \"238 Sixth Street  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"seen\": \"her husband's spirit constantly with her  <<her hus- bands spirit is constantly with her>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"explained  <<Her chief hallucination>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street  <<lodging-house at 238 Sixth Street>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<lodging-house>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<238 Sixth street>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Mrs. Allie Gender  <<Mrs. Allie Gender>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 2: 20_1879-04-11_pna_sn83032041_00212477710_1879041101_0201.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['seen']\n=== 20_1879-04-11_pna_sn83032041_00212477710_1879041101_0201.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f642f18b09e871d4da8bd52d.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/54f207c0d773976b42ca1f82.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f3b9a02de861bff2f7081e3f.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2d9adca2e7e37842d40cfec5.jpg']\nheadline: \"THE HAUNTED HOUSE,\n\n4 Strange hut True story Related by\n\n\nDan J. Garrity i'm Boston Pilot.\n---\nThe time OF my narrative dates back\nto the year 1870. The events occurred\nin the city of Springfield. Ohio.\n\n\nSituated in the very centre of the city\nwas a mansion. old and lonely in aspect.\nthe property of a Mr.. FoOs. 1t had been\nfor several years Uninhabited. when\nstrange reports began to circulate Per\nsons who passed there at midnight, and\nother uncanny hours, often saw strange\nlights and heard stranger sounds, until\npeople believed that it was haunted.\n\n\nAt length two young men of the town\nresolved to see whether it was haunted\nor not, and thus put the fears and gOS-\nsipings of the towns people to an end.\n\n\nAccordingly they took up their quar-\ntiers at the mansion. About eight\nO'Clock they lit their candles, and made\nthemselves comfortable to receive their\nghoStly visitors.\n\n\nThe clock struck nine, ten, eleven. and\nit was now nearly twelve O'Clock. the\ntime for ghosts to appear. The great\nclock in st. Raphael's church began to\nstrike one. two, three. four, five, six.\nseven, eight. nine, ten, eleven, t,reIre.\nand then-No sooner had the sOnorous\npeals died away. than the candles were\nsuddenly OXtnguiShed. and they were\nleft in darkness. After a few minutes\nbright. circular light became visible\nnear one of the walls, and what terrible\nspectacle was brought to view \\ man\nwas stretched from tree with a rope\naround his neck. while a box lay at his\nfeet within reach-he was a suicide\n/ His distorted features and glaring eyes\nwere plainly visible, while his tongue.\nblack and swollen. hung at least half a\nfoot from his month To complete the\nhorrible picture. hundreds of demons\ntod\nThen followed wild burst of laughter\nand the apparition vanished.\nThe young men had not expected this.\nWhile this strange scene was enactmg\nthey sat stUpefied with fear, their hair\nactually standing on end.\n\n\nAt length their horrible spell was\nbroken, and without even stopping to\nsnatch their hats, they fled the house\nAs they were fleeing along the street.\nthey ran right into the arms of tall,\nmuScUlaTman, who seeing their alright\ned condition. frightened his grasp upon\nthem, and asked them to explain their\nfright.\n\n\nThey told him all.\n\n\nAfter they had finished their story,\nthe detective for it was no other than\nDetective John Burnside. of New \\ Ork.\nwho was visiting friends there told\nthem Ito say nothing about it, but wait\nand hope and he would discover the\nmystery if possible\n\n\nAbout two weeks after the detective\nreturned hOme-so his friends thought.\n\n\nIn course of time the young men dis\ncovered that they conld no longer keep\nthe secret. and 50 they divulged it.\n\n\n1t raised great excitement, of course,\nand the people Of the city gave the place\na wide berth.\n\n\nThe strange sounds and sights We're\ncontinued. until the people believed\nwithout a doubt that the house was\nhaunted.\n\n\nWe Will pass over year.\n\n\nOne morning a posse of police, headed\nby Il tall man in plain clothes, approach\ned the FuOs mansion. unlocked the door,\nand passed in.\n\n\nIn a few minutes the sound of pistol\nShots was heard. and then all was still.\nIn few minutes the posse emerged from\nthe house. looking much larger. What\ncould il mean\n\n\nAnd now, little Ants. my narrative is\nat an end, and Detective Burnside will\nfinish the story.\n\n\nNARRATIVE by DETECTIVE BURN\n\n\nSIDE.\n\n\nAfter | left the two young men, said\nDetective Burnside afterwards in telling\nthe story. my mind was made up\nwould discover the mystery.\n\n\nAccordingly. the next evening. | pro-\nceeded to the mansion. It was a mere\nrepetition OF the story of the young men,\nas far as the apparitiOn. As soon as the\nclock struck twelve my candle was\nblown ont by gust Of wind | know.\ncaused by the slamming of doors. And\nwhat a terrible sight met my eye. |\nshudder now when | think of it, 50 ter\nribly real it looked.\n\n\nThere in the same spot that the young\nmen had described | saw young and\nbeautiful girl on her knees \\ form\nwas bending over her. its hand clas ped\nher long golden hair, while a keen.\nbloody knife was drawn across her fair\nwhite throat, while torrents of crimson\nblood dripped down upon the floor.\n\n\n| regained by self-posseSSion enough tC\ndraw my pistol. aim. and fire. y wild\nlaugh followed. and my bullet was heard\ncrashing through the wainscoting.\nThe apparition vanished slowly. anC\nhappening to turn around discovered\nthe mystery.\n\n\n1t was gang of some sort. / wa:\nsure, and | was resolved to capture\nthem. A few weeks after | joined tn,\ngang. 10y means known only to myself\na professional secret. There were coun\n, terfeiters, burglars. and everything els'\n, among them. I Will not weary the read\n\n\neT with a description of the numerOu\n\n\nburglaTieS they committed. or of the va\n\n\nrious WAYS in which they manufacture,\n= and - showed their queer money\ne After staying with them for about\nt year, | resolved to break up the gang\n2 for l had now ample evidence to convic\nD them.\n\n\ne Accordingly. l obtained the posse q\n+ police. and raided the house. After\ne slight resistance they were captured.\nI When they found out who their cap\n2 tor was they threatened me with ven\nI geance dire, if they ever escaped bu\n+ they never did, for there was not one c\n' them but had committed enough crime\n+ TO condemn them for life.\nIS \\ few weeks after the gang We're sen\n4 to prison ! took opportunity to sho'\nG some visitors the house, and explain tn\nq secret of the ghosts In ther room whel\nV the apparitiOn\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"4 Strange hut True story Related by\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6,\n  7,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"printed as a true story from the Boston Pilot, though told to children; a gang's magic lantern; merged with an item on a shoemaker's stone\",\n \"place\": \"the Foos mansion, Springfield, Ohio  <<in the city of Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Ohio  <<Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a bright circular light, and apparitions of a hanged man and a murdered girl  <<bright. circular light became visible>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<away by means of a magic lantern>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Foos mansion  <<the property of a Mr.. FoOs>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<was a mansion. old and lonely in aspect>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the property of a Mr.. FoOs>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"persons who passed at midnight  <<Per sons who passed there at midnight>>\",\n  \"two young men of the town  <<two young men of the town>>\",\n  \"Detective John Burnside  <<Detective John Burnside>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"until people believed that it was haunted\",\n \"rules\": [\n  6,\n  7,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"merged; signals conflict, the text's own framing ('A Strange but True Story') decides\",\n \"place\": \"Springfield, Ohio  <<the city of Springfield. Ohio>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Ohio  <<Ohio>>\",\n \"seen\": \"strange lights and stranger sounds  <<saw strange lights and heard stranger sounds>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<they frightened thel e away by means of a magic lantern>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Foos mansion  <<the FuOs mansion>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<a mansion>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the FuOs mansion>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"persons who passed there at midnight  <<Per sons who passed there at midnight>>\",\n  \"two young men of the town  <<two young men of the town>>\",\n  \"Detective John Burnside  <<Detective John Burnside>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 3: 22_1914-08-24_pna_sn88085187_00211108381_1914082401_0591.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 22_1914-08-24_pna_sn88085187_00211108381_1914082401_0591.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/dc1cfa0456713bf97ab95035.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/288d846c03b2ae64a034c13f.jpg']\nheadline: The Parental School\n---\nAn inspection of the Parental School, supervised\nby the local school board, forcefuly impresses the\nvisitor that the 20-odd lads confined therein are\nas matter of fact, enjoying vastly better home in\nfluenee than perhaps one-half the boys who live\nwith their parents Mr.. and Mrs. John c. Greene,\nIn charge of the school, young folk. Greene who\nis head -master, farm boss, companion and robust\nvithal is young enough to have the boys viewpoint.\nPersonally If boy again, we would be\nstrongly tempted to hook jack and thrust out an i'm\npudent tongue at the truant officer and devise other\ndevilish means, to enjoy few months at the Parent\nal school, it is conducted in Tacoma. Once boy\nhas been judge \"ineorrigble,' the best way, sane\nauthorities agree, to improve him is to strengthen\nhis spirit, not to break it, 'tIncorrigbty' in boys\nIs another and more awsesome term for BOYS who\nnot milksops. We hazard the guess that Huclxleber\nry Finn, and Teddy Roosevelt and Henry Ford and\nsuch, were \"incorrigibles' in their day.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe direct primary is great advertising medium\nSome of these county candidates may not get any\nvotes, except from their family, but they had\ntheir pictures every fence and tree in the city for\nweeks.\n\n\nTacomas police force is getting desperate 1t be-\ngan Saturday night to arrest motorcycles and auto\nmobiles. Wonder why we don't hear of 'em pinch\ning some of the dives that Mavor Faweett has ex-\nposed and reported to Mills and Loomisg\n\n\nChief of Police Ardella p LOOMS openly defies\nthe mayor to prove charges of graft But he ceverlv\nmentions in his interview that if there is graft in\nthe police department he doesn't know anything\nshout it. The coppers ought to feel gratfied toward\ntheir boss for the inuendo supplied in the statement\n\n\nCongressman johnson doesn't feel that he can\nleave Washington to do a little fenee-budng IN his\ndistrict All of which goes to show that johnson has\nmore sense than believed he had The money\nthat he would spend on the trip and campaign will\ncome IN handy when be retires from congress next\nspring\n\n\narmy EngIand's to get $4,000 dozen American eggs\nat pc the Dozen\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"The direct primary is great advertising medium\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"editorial paragraphs; spirit and medium in their ordinary senses\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"to strengthen his spirit, not to break it\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10,\n  16\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\",\n  \"E11\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"merged: editorial paragraphs; spirit and advertising medium in non-ghost senses.\"\n}\n\n##### 4: 29_1909-12-27_pna_sn92053934_00202198764_1909122701_0152.json  kinds=['other', 'advert'] fields=[]\n=== 29_1909-12-27_pna_sn92053934_00202198764_1909122701_0152.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/2a06a6cfc26aaf958bb9393c.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/ebfad0e4f1e8d4003e0fbda7.jpg']\nheadline: The Society of Spiritual Truth.\n\n\nFREE! FREE!\n1O4H West Second street.\n---\nSpiritual meeting Sunday evening\nSpirit message demonstrating immortal\nity. Tests will be given. Doors open 7\np. m. Lecture and tests p. m. Ladies\nand gentlemen welcome. Your departed\nspirit friends viii talk to you through\nthe medium. Seats free. No collections.\nLeClaire Hall, Davenport, Iowa\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"Your departed spirit friends viii talk to you through the medium.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  4\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E5\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a society's notice of a meeting with messages, for later\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"advert\",\n \"kq\": \"Seats free. No collections.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  12\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E5\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"spiritualist meeting notice promising messages through a medium\"\n}\n\n##### 5: 2_1909-04-08_p1_sn86058226_00271744729_1909040801_0067.json  kinds=['fiction', 'report'] fields=[]\n=== 2_1909-04-08_p1_sn86058226_00271744729_1909040801_0067.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/69c54811f79a1256e92c34e5.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b1bc059efa8d6e8b1807fbf4.jpg']\nheadline: A Ghost In q Clock.\n---\nBasingstoke provides 4 remarkable\nstory Of ghost in the form Of q clock.\nAt the approach Of midnight each\nnight the otherwise peaceful grand\nfather'' becomes inhabited by 4 spook.\nThe ticking changes into 4 deep and\npeculiar humping, the clock increases\nIn stature. while a pair Of gray feet\nprotrude from beneath its base. Pass\ning through transitional stages the\nhumping il replaced by q spasmodic\nbreathing. and upon the stroke OF IL\nthe pendulum door opens, revealing an\nenormous ashy gray hand with NAL.\nshaped fingers. The clock face dis\nappears, displaying q frightful gray\nhead. large and round, with abnormal.\n\" long. pale blue eyes. Beyond a\nquiet stroll. which causes weird tap\npings along the landings during the\nnight. the appariticn il inolfensive and\nis said to prove Of great service In\nsending every one early to bed.-Lon-\ndon Tit Bits.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"fiction\",\n \"kq\": \"Ghost In q Clock.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  8\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E7\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a Tit-Bits jest ab