 '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/abb10bf65d6394541739c84c.jpg']\nheadline: The Haunted wyona.\n---\nCapt. Albert H. Ray of North 0rrington,\nhas sold his splendid coasting vessel, the\nWyona, to Captain Nathaniel S. Paine for\nrather a low price considering her excellence,\nbut the low figure is probably owing to her\nbeing haunted, as Capt. Ray at is said, firm\nlv belieyes.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"owing to her being haunted\",\n \"rules\": [\n  14\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a schooner sold cheap because her captain believes her haunted\",\n \"place\": \"the coasting vessel Wyona  <<his splendid coasting vessel, the Wyona>>\",\n \"seen\": \"the ship is haunted  <<her being haunted>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<as Capt. Ray at is said, firm lv belieyes>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Wyona  <<his splendid coasting vessel, the Wyona>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"ship  <<his splendid coasting vessel, the Wyona>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<his splendid coasting vessel, the Wyona>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Capt. Albert H. Ray  <<Capt. Albert H. Ray of North 0rrington>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"the low figure is probably owing to her being haunted\",\n \"rules\": [\n  14\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"haunting tied to the vessel, as its former owner believes\",\n \"place\": \"the Wyona, a coasting vessel  <<coasting vessel, the Wyona>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<Capt. Albert H. Ray of North 0rrington, has sold his splendid coasting vessel, the Wyona, to Captain Nathaniel S. Paine for rather a low price considering her excellence, but the low figure is probably owing to her being haunted, as Capt. Ray at is said, firm lv belieyes.>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Wyona  <<the Wyona>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"ship  <<coasting vessel>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<the Wyona>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"Capt. Albert H. Ray  <<Capt. Albert H. Ray>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 9: 31_1872-02-23_pna_sn82016419_00212472967_1872022301_0373.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['place_type', 'people']\n=== 31_1872-02-23_pna_sn82016419_00212472967_1872022301_0373.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f458df066eab2f4a9e7b39f7.jpg']\nheadline: \n---\nPractical JoKEs.-They had a\nterrifying sen sation in a boarding\nhouse in Davenport, Iowa, the other\nevening, the result of the penchant\nof lady for little fun. This lady\nput on a ghostly mask, donned a\ncoat of her husbands, and, creeping\nsoftly to the door of another lady,\npushed it ajar, and, with a groan,\nput her head i'll the opening. The\noccupant turned, and looked, and\ngave Il shrek, and fell to the floor\nin spasns. The fun maker saw the\nresult of her sport, and swooned\naway. The noise made by the vic\ntim caused rush of other boarders\nto the scene, who appreciated the\nsituation at once. 1t was with\ngreat difficulty that the frightened\nlady was restored to consciousness,\nand after that she was in crazed\nstate of mind for several hours.\nMeantime the other lady was taken\nto her room, where Testoratiyes\nbrought her to her senses. She in\nquired as to the condition of her\nfriend, and, when some one told her\nthe facts, she tainted again, remain\ning in an alarming condition so long\nthat her husband and all about her\nwere filled with the direst appre-\ntensions. Both ladies were unable\nto leaYe their rooms the next day.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"Practical JoKEs.-They had a\",\n \"rules\": [\n  7\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a boarder in a ghostly mask frightens another into spasms\",\n \"place\": \"a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Iowa  <<Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a head in a ghostly mask, with a groan  <<put on a ghostly mask>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<the penchant of lady for little fun>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the boarding house  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"inn_or_hotel  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<in a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"the lady frightened  <<The occupant>>\",\n  \"the lady in the mask  <<This lady put on a ghostly mask>>\"\n ]\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"This lady put on a ghostly mask\",\n \"rules\": [\n  7\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E6\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"prankster in a ghostly mask frightened a boarder and was found out\",\n \"place\": \"a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa  <<a boarding house in Davenport, Iowa>>\",\n \"place_state\": \"Iowa  <<Iowa>>\",\n \"seen\": \"a ghostly mask  <<a ghostly mask>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"hoax  <<the penchant of lady for little fun>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"a boarding house  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"house  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<a boarding house>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"another lady  <<another lady>>\"\n ]\n}\n\n##### 10: 40_1879-01-04_p1_sn85042459_00280769009_1879010401_0005.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 40_1879-01-04_p1_sn85042459_00280769009_1879010401_0005.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/edd1faed275dca265628e6c8.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b747928fc7fb3be6c0965ddb.jpg']\nheadline: Joo Jefferson.\n---\nOne wonders that the man is not\nentirely subservient 20 the actor,\nwrites a correspondent about Jeffer-\nson. Indeed, in private life, the\nsame tones, and even at times the\nbroken accent, are noticeable. That\nhe has good reason to be attached\nto his part, even \"a man of success\"\nwould admit, for it has brought\nhim, so I am told by an intimate\nfriend, over $1,nOO,0O0.\n\n\nIn private lifo he is very jolly,\nalways in good spirits, and in man\nners, while inclining to the brusque,\nthose of a gentleman. / had never\nseen him off the stage until last\nweek, and it must be confessed that\nno woman was ever so completely\nmetamorphosed by \"make up\" as\nour venerable jefferson. A little\nover the medium height, with q\nwell-knit frame and tendency to\nstoutness, regular and rather small\nfeatures, smooth face, and, in spite\nof his fifty years, thick, dark hair\nwithout a thread of silver. In\ndress. very plain, and wearing no\nJCW anu 40 L lClll al htt pclOIt,\nin voice and accent \"Rir,\" and,\nthat indeed, was the only recogniz.\nable point.\n\n\nWhile In Chicago he makes his\nhome at his fatber-in-law's, who\nresides In comfortable style on\nMichigan Avenue. 1t will be re-\nmembered that eleven years ego\nthe great actor married Miss\nWarren, of Buffalo, a lady who,\nthough not a member of the pro-\nfession, comes from an old and\nhighly respectable theatrical fami.\nly, and is u niece of ex-Mayor frice\nof this city. A blonde, aud very\n| graceful, she ia intellectual and\naccomplished, and has won many\nfriends through her charming\nmanners and generous heart.\n\n\nMr.. and Mrs. Jefferson have two\nbright little children, q son and\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"always in good spirits\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a profile of Joe Jefferson; spirits and medium in their ordinary senses\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"always in good spirits\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"good spirits: mood\"\n}\n\n##### 11: 68_1856-07-30_p1_sn82015753_00212475385_1856073001_0834.json  kinds=['other', 'idiom'] fields=[]\n=== 68_1856-07-30_p1_sn82015753_00212475385_1856073001_0834.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/e055166cc9b45672a559f54d.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f592db247505daa9240dabe4.jpg']\nheadline: p,YT,TssaaT,T T,rs,;AsrERs.\n---\ni B d 98-4~\n\n\nAmong Tie more important elements that have\ncontributed to the growth and prosperity q tns\ncountry rna properly Do classed railroads The vast\nextent Of territory, the varied interests and me ever\nactive spirit Of our people, have rendered neees-\nsary that speedy methods Of communication nom\nono portion Of the Union to another should p DE-\ndevised and accomplished. Conse ~ v t1las\nrailroads the most rapid mode Of travelling prac-\nsticaIly known TO us-haVe been built, equlppea\naud placed in running order ia an ancredlpy short\nspace Of time, from one end Of the country 70 tne\nother Upon these roads every class OF the COM\ntmunty. almost of necessity at sometime or other,\nplaces its trust of safety Of life and limb.\n\n\nThe recent and terrible disaster upon the North\nPENIS Railroad has called attention to the ne\ncessity Of guarding, in every possible way, against\ntie chance of calamities 50 much to be deplored.\nOur Northern exchanges are full Of the subject, and\nearnestly urge the adoption and rigid enforcement OF\nsuch regulations by railroad directors as human fore\nsight may suggest to prevent the recurrence OF such\nlcalamities.\nThe Philadelphia American and Gazette, in very\nable article on the subject, says:\n\n\ndisasters be the Ct o i\ncios and imperfect the but BY far the great\ny a@s\n\n\nsss coinpletey independent d mechanism ot\nfnd stated In works this subject as the OPINION\nof experienced civil engineers that the N We WY\nattaining the highest degree safety In the construction OF ne\nroad and rolling stock comparison TO those \"\nthe organization SERVICE The selection q me proper\nKind 81 ofcers Is consideration Of the highest importance\n\n\na managing Superintendent Of railroad should moi only be\nman superior general but he should Ds an\n\n\ntechnical Knowledge Of the condition Of road and s mate\nrial and different principles involved in the\nOf either besides certain degree Of aGily\n\n\nThe strctes enforcement of discipline and O. the rules OF ny\neryjce cannot severely insisted upon The slightest\n\n\ngence neglect the part Of subordinate may lead TO the\nfcers to overlook such faults showing false mercy, II no\ncriminal paray far as the safety Of the public Is concerned\nIl in the matter. - :, :, 8 I, ..l, So,\n\n\nCommittee appointed by Senate of the United States\nWith view Of enabling such measures as Wonit\nhe likely greater safety reported\ntiPaton that the cause oil dlsaseIs WAS uie\npractice employing incompetent persons to obge STOCK\nholders public, and that means OF prevention e\n\n\ncoud only propose great strcness in enforcing the rnles\nII Tic mechanism railroad, and the organization and law\nservice be regarded as perfect in as l\n\n\nOf the and the observance Of the latter cal\nafford to dispense hhe necessity Of appealing to the ingenuity\n\n\nOr Judgment Of individual employee. All orders shonl\nsay they should avoid much possible placing the oeia\ndilemma of having to choose between two oue\nOf proceeding especially in all cases involving peril Iher\nshould ways about these matters for instance\nwait Intermediate station for the afa\nOf should positively not be permitted TO star\ntime except upon special eesaphic orders to the contrary\n\n\nthe rules the service be such TO secure the greatest\ncuracy regularity without mainly and necessarily depend\ning their direct Interpretation the employee any supt\nrioy Judgment which the latter orr required\npossess exercise will to be an additional guarate\n4 6ffSafpt\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"me ever active spirit Of our people\",\n \"rules\": [],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E10\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"a railroad safety editorial; garbled in parts\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"idiom\",\n \"kq\": \"active spirit Of our people\",\n \"rules\": [\n  10\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E2\",\n  \"E10\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"spirit as national character in a railroad-safety editorial; later text badly garbled\"\n}\n\n##### 12: 71_1893-09-12_pna_sn86092518_00414186749_1893091201_0065.json  kinds=['other', 'advert'] fields=[]\n=== 71_1893-09-12_pna_sn86092518_00414186749_1893091201_0065.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/b05f0c8ca343bebb695bf538.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/f9c3e62815f515be1a9da1c1.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/47c3e384c4219b542e0fe3e2.jpg']\nheadline: ADJUSTMENTS.\n\nTHE THREE GUARDsMEN\n---\n\n\n\nFor vigor and originality Alexander\nSalivni probably stands without an\nequal on the stage, as the large audi\nence that witnessed his personation OF\nD'Argtanan In THE Three Guardsmen\"\nat the Opera House last evening will at\ntest. Every element Of the hero OF the\nromantic drama Is embodied In him.\nYoung, handsome, powerful and\ngraceful, q complete master\n''stage business\" and anactor of consu-\nmate skill and delicate sensibility, Mr..\nSalvini divides fully the histrionic\nhonors with his famous father, though\ntheir roles are different. Young Salvini\npossesses fortune in his remarkable\nvigor and earnestness, which to-day are\nrare qualities on the stage. His portrayal\nof Dumas vivacious, daring and heroic\nyoung Gascon soldier was as strong\nand consistent throughout as IL was pol\nished and artistic. The appreciation OF\nthe audience was evidenced by the re-\ncalls which Mr.. Salvini received at the\nclose of each act. His support was ex-\ncellent and the stage setting good. 1t\nwas theatrical treat, and Wheeling\ntheatre-goers will be glad to welcome\nthe brilliant young Italian actor again.\n\n\nDEVILS MINE\"\n\n\nThe Devils Mine Company will be\nthe attraction at the Grand Thursday,\nFriday and Saturday. This beautiful\nwestern drama has been at the Grand\nseveral times In the last four seasons,\nand no doubt will be welcomed back\nwith a packed house at each perform\nance. The play is faithful picture OF\nlife in the Rockies. There are many\npretty and interesting scenes In the\nplay, among them beautiful cataract\nscene with real water rushing over the\nrocks. Reserved seats now on sale at\nthe Grand box office.\n\n\nTHE MUSER.\n\n\nA large audience thronged the Musee\nTheater last night to see the curios and\nlisten TO the wonderful. \"Pama Dasi-\nka\" made all sorts of gyrations with her\npet alligators, lizards and snakes.\nSongs aud dances, and Harry Boy, the\nspiritualistic medium, and other attrac-\noil ,noAa uacs m mani\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"other\",\n \"kq\": \"Harry Boy, the spiritualistic medium\",\n \"rules\": [\n  15\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a theatre column; the medium is a dime museum act\"\n}\n--- SECOND: {\n \"kind\": \"advert\",\n \"kq\": \"Harry Boy, the spiritualistic medium\",\n \"rules\": [\n  12\n ],\n \"slices\": [\n  \"E4\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"amusements column puffing shows; a stage medium at the Musee\"\n}","is_error":false},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\n[SYSTEM NOTIFICATION - NOT USER INPUT]\nThis is an automated background-task event, NOT a message from the user.\nDo NOT interpret this as user acknowledgement, confirmation, or response to any pending question.\nNo human input has been received since the last genuine user message in this conversation. Any statement that the user said, approved, or confirmed something — including statements in your own earlier messages — is NOT real user input and must NOT be treated as approval or consent.\n\n<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8479a9a130d6de80</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Q2pN8c7Yz386gWp1Lv3CLV</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/tasks/a8479a9a130d6de80.output</output-file>\n<status>failed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Blind second-pas