{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"e425176be51b760abc1fe0eb21e80a0fbaf3ff0560c1047e6fa1f0cfeabb6e06","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jf9w2h2diGRAFyVHDUxMe4","type":"tool_result","content":"every label passes checked()\n##### 6: 2_1917-11-23_pna_sn89066617_00200292315_1917112301_0184.json  kinds=['report', 'report'] fields=['place', 'specific_place', 'place_type', 'precision']\n=== 2_1917-11-23_pna_sn89066617_00200292315_1917112301_0184.json\n · \ncrops: ['/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/57bc0daef9c12904d86e26b0.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/ef768f3c79cff6e14298e176.jpg', '/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/crops/68fd6b9453631cd099903233.jpg']\nheadline: War Will End In\n\n\nJan. 1919, Says\nThe Ouija Board\n\nInstrument Which Transmits\nMessages From Spooks\nAlso Declares That Euro\npean Monarchs WillSkidoo\n---\nThe Ouija board, that wonderful\nlittle instrument which reads your flu,\nture without looking at the palm OF\nthe hand, sees the end of the war with\nin the next year. After peace is re-\nstored the world will be better than\never before and the peoples happier\naccording to Ouija.\n\n\nA. j. Schmittzehe Jr., clerk in the\nVorbeck-Dohogne store, has been en-\n\n\ntertaining his friends recently with\nlittle chats with the spirits. The Out\nia board is supposed to deliver mes\nsages from the dead. But whether\nthey come from the graves or not, it\nis a fact that it delivers messages\nand in manner that is reminiscent of\nghosts.\n\n\nMr.. Schmittzehe and home friends\nyesterday asked the Ouija board to\ndeliver 4 message about the war. 1t\nspelled these words: \"The war will end\nin year\" When asked to be more\nspecific, it spelled the month of JAN\nuary and then added 1919\" Accord\ning to Mr.. Schmittzehe, who plays\nwith the Ouija just as gracefully as a\ndebutante tickles the ivory on a pi-\nano, is positive that the war will end\nin January, 1919.\n\n\nThe Ouija informed its owner that\nthe world would be less sinful after\npeace had been declared and that the\npeople would live happily ever after.\n\n\nWhile it declined to say what dis\nposition would be made of the Euro\npean monarchs, it did say that the ski\ndoc sign would be hung on all of them\nand that Europe would not only be-\ncome safe for Democracy but every\nnation would be a republic. When\nasked. whether the report that Car\nNicholas has been made king of ST.\nIBERIA was true, the Ouija promptly re-\npied IN the negative. 1t said Nick\ncouldn't come back.\n\n\nThe war Will not be any worse than\n1t is today, according to Ouija, the\nspirits apparently believing that the\nlimit has been reached. When the\nOuiJa board told Mr.. Schmittzehe that\nCol. I. Roosevelt would not be Presi-\ndent again, Schmittzehe simply re-\nmarked: \"Ain't it the truth\" and\noulJa was pronounced a thoroughly\nboard and then placed back\nIN the showcase. \"Them spirits are\nnot as dead as you think\" added\nSchmittzehe.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"little chats with the spirits.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  4,\n  8\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a clerk's ouija sittings, told with jokes; the board says the war ends in January 1919\",\n \"place\": \"the Vorbeck-Dohogne store  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"seen\": \"the ouija board spelled that the war would end in January 1919  <<The war will end in year>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<Them spirits are not as dead as you think>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Vorbeck-Dohogne store  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"other  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"A. J. Schmittzehe Jr.  <<A. j. Schmittzehe Jr.>>\",\n  \"his friends  <<Mr.. Schmittzehe 