t as gracefully as a\ndebutante tickles the ivory on a pi-\nano, is positive that the war will end\nin January, 1919.\n\n\nThe Ouija informed its owner that\nthe world would be less sinful after\npeace had been declared and that the\npeople would live happily ever after.\n\n\nWhile it declined to say what dis\nposition would be made of the Euro\npean monarchs, it did say that the ski\ndoc sign would be hung on all of them\nand that Europe would not only be-\ncome safe for Democracy but every\nnation would be a republic. When\nasked. whether the report that Car\nNicholas has been made king of ST.\nIBERIA was true, the Ouija promptly re-\npied IN the negative. 1t said Nick\ncouldn't come back.\n\n\nThe war Will not be any worse than\n1t is today, according to Ouija, the\nspirits apparently believing that the\nlimit has been reached. When the\nOuiJa board told Mr.. Schmittzehe that\nCol. I. Roosevelt would not be Presi-\ndent again, Schmittzehe simply re-\nmarked: \"Ain't it the truth\" and\noulJa was pronounced a thoroughly\nboard and then placed back\nIN the showcase. \"Them spirits are\nnot as dead as you think\" added\nSchmittzehe.\n--- FIRST: {\n \"kind\": \"report\",\n \"kq\": \"little chats with the spirits.\",\n \"rules\": [\n  4,\n  8\n ],\n \"slices\": [],\n \"note\": \"a clerk's ouija sittings, told with jokes; the board says the war ends in January 1919\",\n \"place\": \"the Vorbeck-Dohogne store  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"seen\": \"the ouija board spelled that the war would end in January 1919  <<The war will end in year>>\",\n \"outcome\": \"unknown  <<Them spirits are not as dead as you think>>\",\n \"specific_place\": \"the Vorbeck-Dohogne store  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"place_type\": \"other  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"precision\": \"building  <<clerk in the Vorbeck-Dohogne store>>\",\n \"people\": [\n  \"A. J. Schmittzehe Jr.  <<A. j. Schmittzehe Jr.>>\",\n  \"his friends  <<Mr.. Schmittzehe 